1
00:00:00,852 --> 00:00:02,621
(Ito Junji)

2
00:00:02,622 --> 00:00:04,992
(I'll get you a meeting with him.)

3
00:00:06,392 --> 00:00:08,962
(Thus began...)

4
00:00:09,192 --> 00:00:12,192
(Kian84's journey to meet his role model.)

5
00:00:13,632 --> 00:00:17,102
(He's been studying Japanese for this day.)

6
00:00:19,742 --> 00:00:21,341
(He even prepared boxed meals with a lot of love.)

7
00:00:21,342 --> 00:00:22,342
(Pressing)

8
00:00:22,642 --> 00:00:23,742
(Satisfied)

9
00:00:24,142 --> 00:00:25,271
(And...)

10
00:00:25,272 --> 00:00:26,942
(Kian84 prepared...)

11
00:00:27,682 --> 00:00:29,111
(To me, Ito Junji...)

12
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:31,552
(reminds me of space...)

13
00:00:31,652 --> 00:00:33,252
(and a black hole.)

14
00:00:39,922 --> 00:00:43,262
(His sincere admiration toward his role model)

15
00:00:43,592 --> 00:00:46,162
(At last, he's about to meet...)

16
00:00:46,302 --> 00:00:49,672
(his role model.)

17
00:00:50,472 --> 00:00:53,572
(The most nerve-racking moment)

18
00:00:54,402 --> 00:00:56,372
(Utterly nervous)

19
00:00:57,772 --> 00:01:01,282
(He finally enters the meeting place.)

20
00:01:03,582 --> 00:01:06,522
(He gulps down water as he's nervous.)

21
00:01:08,022 --> 00:01:09,521
(Getting nervous too)

22
00:01:09,522 --> 00:01:11,451
- I'm getting nervous for him. - Same here.

23
00:01:11,452 --> 00:01:12,492
(I'm getting nervous for him.)

24
00:01:14,562 --> 00:01:16,091
You don't look confident at all.

25
00:01:16,092 --> 00:01:17,762
Why did I ask to meet him? That was unnecessary.

26
00:01:18,792 --> 00:01:20,202
I'm getting dizzy. This is bad.

27
00:01:20,762 --> 00:01:22,261
You have to help me. When I'm struggling,

28
00:01:22,262 --> 00:01:24,131
- please help me a lot. - Of course.

29
00:01:24,132 --> 00:01:25,332
I'll try to read the vibe first.

30
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:26,502
(Exhaling)

31
00:01:26,602 --> 00:01:28,341
Imagine going there by yourself without Kangnam.

32
00:01:28,342 --> 00:01:29,971
Gosh, I couldn't have survived.

33
00:01:29,972 --> 00:01:30,972
(Feeling dizzy)

34
00:01:31,612 --> 00:01:35,542
I started to study Japanese...

35
00:01:35,712 --> 00:01:38,012
since the last time I met you.

36
00:01:38,182 --> 00:01:39,252
You improved, though.

37
00:01:39,352 --> 00:01:40,882
- Has it been six months? - Yes.

38
00:01:41,182 --> 00:01:43,221
I've been studying for six months. He's here.

39
00:01:43,222 --> 00:01:44,321
I've been studying for six months.

40
00:01:44,322 --> 00:01:45,792
(Is that a knock on the door?)

41
00:01:46,222 --> 00:01:47,461
- He's here. - He's here.

42
00:01:47,462 --> 00:01:51,391
(Their guest arrives even before they had a chance to relax.)

43
00:01:51,392 --> 00:01:54,601
- Sir. It's nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.

44
00:01:54,602 --> 00:01:56,872
(Nice to meet you.)

45
00:01:57,802 --> 00:01:59,102
You became a boy again.

46
00:02:02,272 --> 00:02:03,441
Sir.

47
00:02:03,442 --> 00:02:05,711
- My goodness. It's really him. - Yes.

48
00:02:05,712 --> 00:02:06,811
(It's really Ito Junji.)

49
00:02:06,812 --> 00:02:07,911
My gosh.

50
00:02:07,912 --> 00:02:09,081
(It's really Ito Junji.)

51
00:02:09,082 --> 00:02:10,652
- I'm getting emotional for him. - Me too.

52
00:02:10,782 --> 00:02:12,281
Go ahead and say hello to him.

53
00:02:12,282 --> 00:02:14,722
(Rushing over)

54
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,591
(A meeting with his role model he dreamed of for a long time)

55
00:02:17,592 --> 00:02:18,792
- My gosh. - Nice to meet you.

56
00:02:19,352 --> 00:02:20,491
This is so surreal.

57
00:02:20,492 --> 00:02:21,622
- It's so surreal. - Yes.

58
00:02:22,592 --> 00:02:24,292
- Here? - You can sit on that side.

59
00:02:26,162 --> 00:02:27,501
Kangnam is a good host.

60
00:02:27,502 --> 00:02:28,962
(Kangnam naturally shows him to his seat.)

61
00:02:30,772 --> 00:02:33,142
(Bowing again)

62
00:02:34,102 --> 00:02:38,212
(Now that his role model is in front of him, his head goes blank.)

63
00:02:38,872 --> 00:02:41,742
Once I met him in person,

64
00:02:42,142 --> 00:02:45,882
it was just a jaw-dropping moment.

65
00:02:46,722 --> 00:02:49,522
I couldn't believe he was right in front of me.

66
00:02:51,222 --> 00:02:53,321
It felt like...

67
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:55,161
(Like a storm, stirring in his heart)

68
00:02:55,162 --> 00:02:57,961
I was meeting someone who felt almost unreal.

69
00:02:57,962 --> 00:02:59,292
That was such a surreal moment.

70
00:02:59,602 --> 00:03:04,102
My gosh. I was just over the moon.

71
00:03:06,472 --> 00:03:07,602
You must have been dazed.

72
00:03:08,142 --> 00:03:10,712
Well, growing up in Korea,

73
00:03:11,112 --> 00:03:14,342
there used to be a book rental shop around my house.

74
00:03:14,782 --> 00:03:16,952
And I borrowed his manga books as a kid.

75
00:03:17,312 --> 00:03:19,111
The fact that I was meeting him...

76
00:03:19,112 --> 00:03:20,351
Meeting him couldn't have been a big deal...

77
00:03:20,352 --> 00:03:21,621
if he had made many public appearances.

78
00:03:21,622 --> 00:03:23,352
- Right. He doesn't. - But he doesn't do that.

79
00:03:23,552 --> 00:03:26,022
- I'm grateful to Kangnam again. - Right.

80
00:03:27,662 --> 00:03:29,562
(Nervous)

81
00:03:30,192 --> 00:03:31,362
So...

82
00:03:32,692 --> 00:03:33,701
(Smiling)

83
00:03:33,702 --> 00:03:35,062
meeting you like this...

84
00:03:36,232 --> 00:03:37,472
feels like a dream.

85
00:03:39,542 --> 00:03:40,702
- Thank you. - It was nice.

86
00:03:41,802 --> 00:03:44,972
(He carefully delivers the introduction he practiced.)

87
00:03:45,312 --> 00:03:47,612
I grew up reading your manga.

88
00:03:48,212 --> 00:03:52,612
I dreamed of becoming a cartoonist...

89
00:03:52,882 --> 00:03:53,952
I see.

90
00:03:54,722 --> 00:03:57,121
(Whispering)

91
00:03:57,122 --> 00:03:58,451
after reading your manga.

92
00:03:58,452 --> 00:03:59,452
(Relieved)

93
00:03:59,453 --> 00:04:00,622
It's an honor.

94
00:04:01,592 --> 00:04:02,692
Do you want to introduce yourself first?

95
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:04,691
- Introduce myself? - You should start with that.

96
00:04:04,692 --> 00:04:05,731
- I should do that. - Yes.

97
00:04:05,732 --> 00:04:07,102
- I am... - Yes.

98
00:04:08,302 --> 00:04:09,402
So...

99
00:04:10,132 --> 00:04:11,501
- I've been a cartoonist... - Yes.

100
00:04:11,502 --> 00:04:13,242
in Korea...

101
00:04:13,442 --> 00:04:16,811
for 10 minutes. No, 10 years.

102
00:04:16,812 --> 00:04:18,112
"For ten minutes."

103
00:04:19,312 --> 00:04:21,542
"I've been drawing cartoons in Korea for ten minutes."

104
00:04:22,082 --> 00:04:24,212
My brain was working at full capacity. I'm serious.

105
00:04:26,482 --> 00:04:29,622
I watched a video about your solo exhibit...

106
00:04:30,152 --> 00:04:32,452
on YouTube.

107
00:04:32,592 --> 00:04:33,762
He watched you on YouTube.

108
00:04:35,222 --> 00:04:39,662
(He's seen my artworks?)

109
00:04:40,132 --> 00:04:42,532
I felt so shy when he said he had seen my work.

110
00:04:42,702 --> 00:04:44,371
He watched a video about your solo exhibit?

111
00:04:44,372 --> 00:04:46,101
He watched a video of our show.

112
00:04:46,102 --> 00:04:47,772
That's right. It's also on YouTube.

113
00:04:48,342 --> 00:04:50,512
- I thought it was cute. - You think he's cute?

114
00:04:51,572 --> 00:04:53,312
- I meant, his art was cute. - His art?

115
00:04:53,542 --> 00:04:54,642
Thank you.

116
00:04:56,142 --> 00:04:58,712
(Not knowing what to do with himself)

117
00:05:00,382 --> 00:05:02,922
There's something I'd like to tell you.

118
00:05:03,692 --> 00:05:07,262
- It was 1994. - Yes.

119
00:05:08,322 --> 00:05:11,462
In front of my house,

120
00:05:12,092 --> 00:05:15,332
there was an old bookstore.

121
00:05:15,702 --> 00:05:17,572
That was where I read...

122
00:05:18,102 --> 00:05:21,341
your manga for the first...

123
00:05:21,342 --> 00:05:22,742
- "Time." - time.

124
00:05:23,512 --> 00:05:25,672
Your manga...

125
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:29,712
had a big influence on my.

126
00:05:29,882 --> 00:05:31,252
It's "on me."

127
00:05:31,812 --> 00:05:33,222
(He makes a series of mistakes as he's nervous.)

128
00:05:33,552 --> 00:05:36,722
I'm sorry. I studied Japanese only for a short time.

129
00:05:36,922 --> 00:05:38,552
- You're very good. - He said you were good.

130
00:05:38,822 --> 00:05:40,122
It's only been six months he began studying.

131
00:05:40,792 --> 00:05:42,962
- But he already speaks so well. - He studied hard.

132
00:05:43,562 --> 00:05:45,891
So to me...

133
00:05:45,892 --> 00:05:47,402
(He only focuses on what to say next.)

134
00:05:47,702 --> 00:05:49,162
you are...

135
00:05:51,272 --> 00:05:52,972
like a white hole?

136
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,602
- A black hole? - Yes, a black hole.

137
00:05:54,772 --> 00:05:57,772
- What are you trying to say? - A black hole...

138
00:05:58,042 --> 00:05:59,712
That's what you are to me. My gosh.

139
00:06:00,512 --> 00:06:01,912
I see. To him,

140
00:06:02,412 --> 00:06:05,452
you're like a black hole in space that draws people in.

141
00:06:06,322 --> 00:06:08,322
(Grateful)

142
00:06:08,722 --> 00:06:10,992
- So I prepared a present. - Okay.

143
00:06:11,522 --> 00:06:12,721
- The painting? - You'll start with the painting?

144
00:06:12,722 --> 00:06:14,322
I bet he's going to love it.

145
00:06:14,722 --> 00:06:17,862
(The night before, he thought about his cosmic-like role model.)

146
00:06:18,492 --> 00:06:20,031
Here's the present.

147
00:06:20,032 --> 00:06:22,462
(Kian84 gives him the portrait he painted with great care.)

148
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:27,042
You did a superb job with it.

149
00:06:27,802 --> 00:06:30,172
- How long did it take? - How long did it take?

150
00:06:30,312 --> 00:06:31,841
Three hours?

151
00:06:31,842 --> 00:06:33,342
- Three hours? - Three hours.

152
00:06:33,582 --> 00:06:36,312
- Excellent. You did a great job. - That's...

153
00:06:38,312 --> 00:06:40,051
That's you from your younger days.

154
00:06:40,052 --> 00:06:41,152
(Feeling proud)

155
00:06:41,282 --> 00:06:43,891
This was already 20 years ago.

156
00:06:43,892 --> 00:06:46,022
- It was 20 years ago. - It was 20 years ago?

157
00:06:46,562 --> 00:06:48,391
I wore the glasses then.

158
00:06:48,392 --> 00:06:50,231
The glasses were from 20 years ago.

159
00:06:50,232 --> 00:06:51,362
He remembers the glasses.

160
00:06:51,492 --> 00:06:53,162
You must've been so happy.

161
00:06:54,062 --> 00:06:57,232
You are still a youngster.

162
00:06:57,902 --> 00:06:58,972
"A youngster?"

163
00:07:00,272 --> 00:07:02,272
- "You still look young." - You still look young.

164
00:07:03,712 --> 00:07:04,871
No.

165
00:07:04,872 --> 00:07:06,341
(Laughing)

166
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,811
I turned 63 years old this year.

167
00:07:07,812 --> 00:07:08,942
He's 63 years old.

168
00:07:09,212 --> 00:07:11,412
(My role model is already that old?)

169
00:07:11,582 --> 00:07:13,781
I'm impressed by how well you captured me in the painting.

170
00:07:13,782 --> 00:07:15,252
You did a great job. He's impressed.

171
00:07:16,152 --> 00:07:21,492
His solo exhibit had excellent paintings of cute faces.

172
00:07:21,662 --> 00:07:24,462
His realistic paintings are great too.

173
00:07:25,392 --> 00:07:26,601
- The thing is, - Right.

174
00:07:26,602 --> 00:07:28,661
hearing compliments...

175
00:07:28,662 --> 00:07:30,902
from the artist I really admired...

176
00:07:31,272 --> 00:07:32,901
- felt amazing. - Of course.

177
00:07:32,902 --> 00:07:34,102
- It's touching. - Yes.

178
00:07:34,602 --> 00:07:36,871
(As they talk about art, he thinks of a question.)

179
00:07:36,872 --> 00:07:39,642
Out of all your characters,

180
00:07:40,582 --> 00:07:44,012
- Souichi is my favorite one. - Really?

181
00:07:44,952 --> 00:07:46,851
(Souichi always has nails in his mouth...)

182
00:07:46,852 --> 00:07:48,152
(because he has an iron deficiency.)

183
00:07:49,382 --> 00:07:50,952
(He's a bit twisted.)

184
00:07:51,622 --> 00:07:54,592
(He reminds me of myself when I was young.)

185
00:07:55,262 --> 00:07:57,061
In my opinion,

186
00:07:57,062 --> 00:07:58,062
(Hesitant)

187
00:07:58,462 --> 00:08:01,132
you might have had similarities to Souichi...

188
00:08:02,102 --> 00:08:05,131
when you were young.

189
00:08:05,132 --> 00:08:07,602
(Perhaps, you were similar to Souichi.)

190
00:08:07,702 --> 00:08:09,302
- That's right. - He said you were right.

191
00:08:09,642 --> 00:08:11,212
- Really? - He was.

192
00:08:11,572 --> 00:08:12,642
You seem to understand him well.

193
00:08:13,142 --> 00:08:14,211
- Really? - You were right.

194
00:08:14,212 --> 00:08:16,912
Souichi was based on what I was like as a kid.

195
00:08:18,352 --> 00:08:19,551
But I wasn't that rebellious.

196
00:08:19,552 --> 00:08:20,981
He wasn't that rebellious, though.

197
00:08:20,982 --> 00:08:22,552
(I see.)

198
00:08:23,082 --> 00:08:24,552
Then,

199
00:08:25,292 --> 00:08:27,962
did you perhaps have...

200
00:08:29,322 --> 00:08:32,432
nails in your mouth?

201
00:08:32,632 --> 00:08:34,401
No, I didn't do that.

202
00:08:34,402 --> 00:08:35,932
(Chuckling)

203
00:08:36,972 --> 00:08:38,931
"Did he have nails in his mouth?"

204
00:08:38,932 --> 00:08:40,342
I was wondering if it was based on his childhood.

205
00:08:40,902 --> 00:08:46,412
I have low blood pressure.

206
00:08:46,812 --> 00:08:49,082
I wondered if it had to do with iron deficiency.

207
00:08:50,412 --> 00:08:55,422
At first, I thought about putting iron marbles in his mouth.

208
00:08:56,022 --> 00:09:00,222
So he could spit them out as weapons.

209
00:09:01,362 --> 00:09:04,262
But I thought nails in his mouth...

210
00:09:05,262 --> 00:09:07,201
would be more interesting.

211
00:09:07,202 --> 00:09:08,232
Low blood pressure...

212
00:09:08,732 --> 00:09:11,472
- He didn't have... - He needed more iron.

213
00:09:11,872 --> 00:09:13,902
- I've never told anyone about it. - He's never...

214
00:09:14,002 --> 00:09:15,272
told anyone about it.

215
00:09:16,742 --> 00:09:21,682
Then where did you get your inspiration for "Uzumaki?"

216
00:09:22,542 --> 00:09:25,051
(He keeps asking questions like a kid who just learned to talk.)

217
00:09:25,052 --> 00:09:27,052
(Listening intently)

218
00:09:27,882 --> 00:09:31,751
Are Yon and Mu still alive?

219
00:09:31,752 --> 00:09:33,691
Then is it their baby?

220
00:09:33,692 --> 00:09:35,122
The baby between Yon and Mu?

221
00:09:35,422 --> 00:09:36,732
You even asked about his cats?

222
00:09:38,032 --> 00:09:39,862
- You wanted to ask him everything. - Yes.

223
00:09:40,032 --> 00:09:41,131
It's not easy to meet him.

224
00:09:41,132 --> 00:09:43,132
- He said everything on his mind. - Yes.

225
00:09:43,532 --> 00:09:47,502
He has so many questions for you. I'm serious.

226
00:09:47,602 --> 00:09:49,672
I guess you had that big of an influence on him.

227
00:09:49,912 --> 00:09:52,012
(Grateful)

228
00:09:52,642 --> 00:09:56,681
He was also number one webtoonist in Korea.

229
00:09:56,682 --> 00:10:00,582
I can't read Korean, so I don't know the plot.

230
00:10:00,752 --> 00:10:03,082
But I've seen his drawings.

231
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:04,751
He said he read your webtoon.

232
00:10:04,752 --> 00:10:05,752
What?

233
00:10:06,292 --> 00:10:08,161
(You even read my webtoon?)

234
00:10:08,162 --> 00:10:09,162
He didn't get the plot,

235
00:10:09,162 --> 00:10:10,162
- but he saw your drawings. - How did he come across it?

236
00:10:10,762 --> 00:10:11,862
He's seen it.

237
00:10:12,262 --> 00:10:13,802
I'm quite embarrassed.

238
00:10:15,262 --> 00:10:16,972
My drawings were awful.

239
00:10:19,032 --> 00:10:20,172
I'm so embarrassed.

240
00:10:20,442 --> 00:10:22,242
What? No way.

241
00:10:22,602 --> 00:10:24,172
- That's an artistic painting. - Look how good he is.

242
00:10:25,072 --> 00:10:26,781
That's an artistic painting.

243
00:10:26,782 --> 00:10:27,941
(Feeling small in front of his idol)

244
00:10:27,942 --> 00:10:29,911
Should I say it was more realistic?

245
00:10:29,912 --> 00:10:31,852
- His drawings were fun to look at. - He said they were fun to look at.

246
00:10:34,222 --> 00:10:35,282
"Am I dreaming?"

247
00:10:35,582 --> 00:10:36,992
It did feel like I was dreaming.

248
00:10:37,592 --> 00:10:39,552
(It left an impression on me.)

249
00:10:40,592 --> 00:10:41,922
- Sir. - Yes.

250
00:10:41,992 --> 00:10:43,122
Would you like...

251
00:10:43,732 --> 00:10:44,961
to eat?

252
00:10:44,962 --> 00:10:46,092
Would you like to eat?

253
00:10:46,232 --> 00:10:47,361
I'm a bit hungry.

254
00:10:47,362 --> 00:10:49,001
He's a bit hungry. He hasn't eaten yet.

255
00:10:49,002 --> 00:10:51,971
I actually cooked...

256
00:10:51,972 --> 00:10:54,471
this morning.

257
00:10:54,472 --> 00:10:55,872
- Really? - He cooked.

258
00:10:56,442 --> 00:10:58,942
(He packed boxed meals for his idol this morning.)

259
00:10:59,272 --> 00:11:02,212
(His best dish, kimchi fried rice)

260
00:11:03,552 --> 00:11:04,581
(As someone who has had his fried rice...)

261
00:11:04,582 --> 00:11:05,711
Gosh, I'm worried about this.

262
00:11:05,712 --> 00:11:07,882
I was more nervous giving him the boxed meal than the painting.

263
00:11:09,782 --> 00:11:12,222
If you don't mind, would you like to eat with us?

264
00:11:12,322 --> 00:11:14,062
- Sure. - Would you like to?

265
00:11:14,862 --> 00:11:17,031
It's cold. I wonder if he will mind.

266
00:11:17,032 --> 00:11:19,162
It looks good. I'm sure it tastes fine.

267
00:11:19,192 --> 00:11:21,032
I was worried because it got cold.

268
00:11:21,202 --> 00:11:23,132
He should have eaten it when it was hot.

269
00:11:23,632 --> 00:11:25,932
(Looking around)

270
00:11:26,402 --> 00:11:28,242
(What's wrong?)

271
00:11:28,542 --> 00:11:29,901
Hey, I forgot chopsticks.

272
00:11:29,902 --> 00:11:31,242
(Things are getting worse.)

273
00:11:31,512 --> 00:11:33,342
- I forgot chopsticks. - I'll go and get them.

274
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:34,911
- No. - No, I'll go and get them.

275
00:11:34,912 --> 00:11:36,111
- You will? - I should go.

276
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,351
Where will you get them?

277
00:11:37,352 --> 00:11:39,082
- I... Really? - No, I'll go.

278
00:11:40,082 --> 00:11:41,352
- Excuse me. - Sure.

279
00:11:41,482 --> 00:11:43,692
He's not usually like that. But he's nervous.

280
00:11:43,752 --> 00:11:44,852
(Chuckling)

281
00:11:45,422 --> 00:11:46,921
I could feel my face getting hot.

282
00:11:46,922 --> 00:11:48,961
- Your face is red. - Yes, it got red.

283
00:11:48,962 --> 00:11:50,762
You're like a guy who's never been on a blind date.

284
00:11:51,532 --> 00:11:53,062
(There will be chopsticks, right?)

285
00:11:55,332 --> 00:11:56,332
Hey, Kangnam.

286
00:11:56,672 --> 00:11:57,801
Does warabasi mean chopsticks?

287
00:11:57,802 --> 00:11:59,802
- It's waribasi. - Waribasi?

288
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,902
(I see. He didn't bring chopsticks.)

289
00:12:03,872 --> 00:12:07,682
(Trying to speak for Kian84 for leaving to find chopsticks)

290
00:12:09,782 --> 00:12:12,681
After we became friends, he only talked about you.

291
00:12:12,682 --> 00:12:14,022
Really?

292
00:12:14,852 --> 00:12:16,022
- Did you get them? - Yes.

293
00:12:16,182 --> 00:12:17,752
- What a relief. - He got them.

294
00:12:18,252 --> 00:12:20,392
This is yours. And this one is his.

295
00:12:22,092 --> 00:12:23,631
- I made this. - Why...

296
00:12:23,632 --> 00:12:24,962
Why did you make this face?

297
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:26,702
Thank you.

298
00:12:28,662 --> 00:12:29,862
Do you make good fried rice?

299
00:12:30,702 --> 00:12:32,401
Fried rice? Gosh, one of the eyes got separated.

300
00:12:32,402 --> 00:12:33,701
(The eyes get separated.)

301
00:12:33,702 --> 00:12:35,271
- My gosh, the eyes. - No!

302
00:12:35,272 --> 00:12:36,942
- No! - My gosh.

303
00:12:37,242 --> 00:12:39,111
- That must hurt. - No!

304
00:12:39,112 --> 00:12:40,682
That has the same vibe as his manga.

305
00:12:40,912 --> 00:12:43,211
- Right. The boxed meal lost an eye. - Yes.

306
00:12:43,212 --> 00:12:44,212
(The grotesque unboxing of the boxed meal)

307
00:12:44,352 --> 00:12:45,852
- One of the eyes got separated. - What?

308
00:12:46,282 --> 00:12:47,722
(He picks up the separated eye.)

309
00:12:47,952 --> 00:12:48,982
(Putting it back)

310
00:12:49,422 --> 00:12:50,692
He's so thoughtful.

311
00:12:51,922 --> 00:12:54,021
(Wait. Is that...)

312
00:12:54,022 --> 00:12:56,562
- Is that a face? - It's a face.

313
00:12:56,892 --> 00:12:58,361
(Ta-da)

314
00:12:58,362 --> 00:13:00,502
I tried to mimic your drawing style.

315
00:13:01,062 --> 00:13:02,162
Thank you for the meal.

316
00:13:02,262 --> 00:13:03,262
Dig in, sir.

317
00:13:03,932 --> 00:13:05,631
(I hope he likes the food.)

318
00:13:05,632 --> 00:13:07,971
I was super worried about the food.

319
00:13:07,972 --> 00:13:09,142
(Glancing)

320
00:13:10,742 --> 00:13:14,512
(He scoops up the food and puts it in his mouth.)

321
00:13:15,582 --> 00:13:17,211
(Stir-Fry84 shared...)

322
00:13:17,212 --> 00:13:19,612
(his kimchi fried rice on the field day.)

323
00:13:20,452 --> 00:13:24,952
(The flavor of the kimchi fried rice made everyone...)

324
00:13:26,992 --> 00:13:32,662
(who bravely tried the food go speechless.)

325
00:13:34,462 --> 00:13:39,132
(Will he be able to speak after trying the food?)

326
00:13:39,832 --> 00:13:42,742
(Heart pounding)

327
00:13:47,482 --> 00:13:49,342
(Please...)

328
00:13:51,912 --> 00:13:53,381
- It's tasty. - It is?

329
00:13:53,382 --> 00:13:55,852
(It's tasty.)

330
00:13:56,022 --> 00:13:57,221
- It is? - Yes.

331
00:13:57,222 --> 00:13:58,222
It's tasty.

332
00:13:58,222 --> 00:13:59,222
(Mumbling)

333
00:14:00,762 --> 00:14:03,592
(He has a bite of the food at ease after getting his feedback.)

334
00:14:03,962 --> 00:14:05,832
- Kian84. This is good. - Yes?

335
00:14:07,002 --> 00:14:08,362
It's a bit chilly.

336
00:14:08,602 --> 00:14:10,331
- Chilly? You mean, "cold." - Cold?

337
00:14:10,332 --> 00:14:12,001
- So the food is cold. - It's okay.

338
00:14:12,002 --> 00:14:14,702
- It's still very tasty. - My gosh.

339
00:14:14,742 --> 00:14:15,872
He said it was tasty even cold.

340
00:14:16,812 --> 00:14:17,942
He's so sweet.

341
00:14:18,472 --> 00:14:19,472
It's fried rice.

342
00:14:19,712 --> 00:14:21,412
- "Fried rice." - This is fried rice.

343
00:14:21,512 --> 00:14:23,582
- It's kimchi fried rice. - So...

344
00:14:24,082 --> 00:14:25,681
it's kimchi fried rice.

345
00:14:25,682 --> 00:14:27,822
- It's kimchi. - Yes, it's kimchi fried rice.

346
00:14:28,352 --> 00:14:34,522
Kimchi doesn't taste good unless it's from Korea.

347
00:14:35,192 --> 00:14:37,232
He said Korean kimchi was tasty.

348
00:14:37,492 --> 00:14:38,562
Where did you get this kimchi?

349
00:14:39,132 --> 00:14:40,202
I got it here.

350
00:14:43,262 --> 00:14:44,571
A convenience store...

351
00:14:44,572 --> 00:14:46,602
- Don't tell him that. - Okay.

352
00:14:46,972 --> 00:14:48,202
"Don't tell him."

353
00:14:48,542 --> 00:14:50,141
- We don't have to correct it. - Right.

354
00:14:50,142 --> 00:14:51,871
- I bet he had no idea. - Exactly.

355
00:14:51,872 --> 00:14:53,041
He thought the kimchi was from Korea.

356
00:14:53,042 --> 00:14:54,812
Let's keep him in the dark.

357
00:14:55,842 --> 00:14:57,212
(Glancing)

358
00:14:57,582 --> 00:14:59,582
(Kian84 checks his reaction.)

359
00:15:00,352 --> 00:15:02,682
(Kian84 has another bite since he likes to enjoy it.)

360
00:15:09,892 --> 00:15:11,391
(A big bite)

361
00:15:11,392 --> 00:15:13,232
- Were you hungry? - Well,

362
00:15:13,732 --> 00:15:15,262
after asking him all the questions I prepared,

363
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:18,371
my head went blank.

364
00:15:18,372 --> 00:15:20,501
- Ask him questions while you eat. - What?

365
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:22,141
In Japan, people talk during meals.

366
00:15:22,142 --> 00:15:23,172
- Really? - Yes.

367
00:15:23,442 --> 00:15:25,612
(Feel free to talk.)

368
00:15:25,942 --> 00:15:28,041
(In that case...)

369
00:15:28,042 --> 00:15:29,512
Is the food...

370
00:15:30,042 --> 00:15:32,181
- tasty? - It's tasty.

371
00:15:32,182 --> 00:15:33,552
- You already asked that. - It's tasty.

372
00:15:33,852 --> 00:15:34,982
I'm nervous.

373
00:15:35,322 --> 00:15:36,351
It's tasty.

374
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,351
I have you to thank for this boxed meal.

375
00:15:38,352 --> 00:15:40,692
- Really? - I tested it on you.

376
00:15:41,592 --> 00:15:43,761
(A good friend who agreed to be a test subject)

377
00:15:43,762 --> 00:15:46,061
- Can you cook it again? - Thank you.

378
00:15:46,062 --> 00:15:48,231
- I want to try the tasty version. - Okay.

379
00:15:48,232 --> 00:15:49,861
- I want the tasty version. - Okay. I'll cook it again.

380
00:15:49,862 --> 00:15:51,501
He was able to cook delicious fried rice...

381
00:15:51,502 --> 00:15:52,932
- Yes. - because he failed previously.

382
00:15:53,872 --> 00:15:55,142
What a relief.

383
00:15:55,772 --> 00:15:56,801
(Kian84 asks a question spontaneously...)

384
00:15:56,802 --> 00:15:57,841
(after making sure he likes the food.)

385
00:15:57,842 --> 00:16:00,912
What are you into these days?

386
00:16:01,582 --> 00:16:03,882
I would get invited to attend events abroad.

387
00:16:04,252 --> 00:16:07,452
Since I can't speak English,

388
00:16:07,552 --> 00:16:09,552
it's a bit uncomfortable.

389
00:16:10,222 --> 00:16:13,352
So I've been studying English every day for five minutes.

390
00:16:14,762 --> 00:16:16,421
I'm studying with Duolingo.

391
00:16:16,422 --> 00:16:17,762
- Duolingo? - Yes.

392
00:16:20,262 --> 00:16:22,532
That app is also famous in Korea.

393
00:16:23,262 --> 00:16:25,272
I've been doing it more than 1,000 days consecutively.

394
00:16:25,302 --> 00:16:27,471
- That's amazing. - He's been very diligent.

395
00:16:27,472 --> 00:16:31,742
Then can you communicate when a foreigner talks to you?

396
00:16:31,812 --> 00:16:33,942
- I can't. - No?

397
00:16:34,282 --> 00:16:38,252
I'm at that age where I easily forget new information.

398
00:16:38,312 --> 00:16:41,021
- It's admirable that he's still... - That's amazing.

399
00:16:41,022 --> 00:16:42,851
- studying even at his age. - Exactly.

400
00:16:42,852 --> 00:16:44,291
That's amazing.

401
00:16:44,292 --> 00:16:46,021
That's not an easy thing to do.

402
00:16:46,022 --> 00:16:47,061
(Amazed by his idol who never stops learning)

403
00:16:47,062 --> 00:16:49,822
What made him cook in the first place?

404
00:16:50,932 --> 00:16:53,262
When I used to draw manga,

405
00:16:53,592 --> 00:16:58,332
I always ate boxed meals by myself.

406
00:16:59,402 --> 00:17:04,472
It wasn't good for my health. So I've been cooking these days.

407
00:17:04,612 --> 00:17:06,542
- You can communicate with him. - Right.

408
00:17:06,612 --> 00:17:08,141
- Yes. - Only about simple things.

409
00:17:08,142 --> 00:17:09,581
- But still. - But still.

410
00:17:09,582 --> 00:17:11,151
Kian84's Japanese improved a lot.

411
00:17:11,152 --> 00:17:12,851
His vocabulary is beyond the beginner level now.

412
00:17:12,852 --> 00:17:13,852
- Right. - Yes.

413
00:17:13,853 --> 00:17:15,951
I practiced that one, though.

414
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,151
- But still. - I practiced it.

415
00:17:17,152 --> 00:17:18,921
Even if you practiced...

416
00:17:18,922 --> 00:17:21,762
Right. Six months ago, you only knew the word for monkey.

417
00:17:22,392 --> 00:17:24,661
(His Japanese improved a lot within 6 months.)

418
00:17:24,662 --> 00:17:26,032
- Right. - Yes.

419
00:17:27,802 --> 00:17:32,302
How is your health?

420
00:17:34,402 --> 00:17:36,802
- I have pain all over my body. - He has pain all over his body.

421
00:17:37,142 --> 00:17:38,571
My knees hurt.

422
00:17:38,572 --> 00:17:40,381
- Your knees? - And my elbows too.

423
00:17:40,382 --> 00:17:42,311
His knees and elbows hurt.

424
00:17:42,312 --> 00:17:43,681
- My back also hurts. - And his back.

425
00:17:43,682 --> 00:17:44,682
His back hurts too?

426
00:17:44,952 --> 00:17:46,211
(Worried)

427
00:17:46,212 --> 00:17:49,652
A few years ago, I got a herniated disc.

428
00:17:50,592 --> 00:17:54,692
My spine is crooked.

429
00:17:54,892 --> 00:17:56,322
- That must hurt. - So it hurts.

430
00:17:56,592 --> 00:17:57,691
He had a herniated disc.

431
00:17:57,692 --> 00:17:58,962
- Oh, no. - He had it.

432
00:17:59,262 --> 00:18:00,462
- So he's not feeling well. - No.

433
00:18:00,702 --> 00:18:02,432
It must be because he has a sedentary job.

434
00:18:02,532 --> 00:18:05,472
Actually, sitting all the time takes a toll on manga artists' health.

435
00:18:05,772 --> 00:18:09,471
I guess that's the case for all manga artists.

436
00:18:09,472 --> 00:18:11,012
It's a tough job.

437
00:18:11,212 --> 00:18:13,072
- It is? - We always have deadlines to meet.

438
00:18:14,312 --> 00:18:16,241
He's just like you. He said it was a tough job.

439
00:18:16,242 --> 00:18:18,381
The pressure of meeting deadlines was exhausting.

440
00:18:18,382 --> 00:18:20,452
(He has the same difficulty as Kian84.)

441
00:18:22,452 --> 00:18:23,922
- Does Kian84... - Yes?

442
00:18:25,692 --> 00:18:27,822
still live alone?

443
00:18:27,962 --> 00:18:30,162
- For now, yes. - For now?

444
00:18:30,262 --> 00:18:31,931
I'm a bit lonely.

445
00:18:31,932 --> 00:18:33,492
- You're lonely. - Right.

446
00:18:33,802 --> 00:18:37,601
I'm sure he will make his future wife happy.

447
00:18:37,602 --> 00:18:41,271
He can make tasty boxed meals like this one.

448
00:18:41,272 --> 00:18:42,542
My goodness.

449
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:45,771
Gosh, what a sweet compliment.

450
00:18:45,772 --> 00:18:47,111
He's so kind.

451
00:18:47,112 --> 00:18:48,142
Thank you.

452
00:18:48,242 --> 00:18:50,482
It feels great to see that he finished everything.

453
00:18:50,882 --> 00:18:52,011
(He won't even leave behind a single rice grain.)

454
00:18:52,012 --> 00:18:53,052
- How touching. - Gosh, he...

455
00:18:53,482 --> 00:18:54,781
This was a lot of food, you know?

456
00:18:54,782 --> 00:18:56,421
I made a lot of food on purpose.

457
00:18:56,422 --> 00:18:57,652
And seeing him finish everything...

458
00:18:59,322 --> 00:19:01,122
- He finished everything. - This was a lot of food.

459
00:19:02,462 --> 00:19:03,662
It was delicious.

460
00:19:04,362 --> 00:19:06,362
I cooked a bit more so as not to run out of food.

461
00:19:06,632 --> 00:19:08,202
- But he finished everything. - Oh, my.

462
00:19:09,062 --> 00:19:10,332
I'm so grateful.

463
00:19:11,202 --> 00:19:12,802
(He finished the fried rice.)

464
00:19:13,032 --> 00:19:14,702
- But he finished everything. - Oh, my.

465
00:19:15,242 --> 00:19:17,371
(Choking up)

466
00:19:17,372 --> 00:19:19,312
- This is the most touching moment. - Right?

467
00:19:19,472 --> 00:19:21,241
- Seriously. I'm... - My gosh.

468
00:19:21,242 --> 00:19:22,911
- I kind of felt bad too. - It didn't matter...

469
00:19:22,912 --> 00:19:24,352
whether it tasted good or not.

470
00:19:24,512 --> 00:19:26,652
I'm getting emotional right now.

471
00:19:26,782 --> 00:19:28,221
I'm sure he was also...

472
00:19:28,222 --> 00:19:30,752
- being considerate. - I think so too.

473
00:19:31,892 --> 00:19:33,291
(After the meal, he gets started on his questions.)

474
00:19:33,292 --> 00:19:34,361
He still has more questions.

475
00:19:34,362 --> 00:19:36,362
(Chuckling)

476
00:19:37,022 --> 00:19:39,031
Lately, I haven't seen...

477
00:19:39,032 --> 00:19:41,831
your manga in Korea.

478
00:19:41,832 --> 00:19:43,601
- I see. Is that so? - Yes.

479
00:19:43,602 --> 00:19:46,202
- I... Right. - Are you working on a new series?

480
00:19:46,502 --> 00:19:47,742
I'm curious about it too.

481
00:19:47,842 --> 00:19:49,872
We haven't seen any new manga from him lately.

482
00:19:50,512 --> 00:19:53,272
Well, I'm working on a new series now.

483
00:19:54,082 --> 00:19:56,882
I finished up to Episode 3 out of 22 episodes.

484
00:19:57,082 --> 00:19:58,311
Gosh, that's amazing.

485
00:19:58,312 --> 00:20:00,152
I thought he was done with drawing manga.

486
00:20:00,452 --> 00:20:02,752
Then do you...

487
00:20:03,322 --> 00:20:06,752
still enjoy drawing manga?

488
00:20:08,762 --> 00:20:10,891
I've been drawing manga on paper, the old-fashioned way,

489
00:20:10,892 --> 00:20:12,431
after a long time.

490
00:20:12,432 --> 00:20:15,561
- That's great. - The joy I used to feel...

491
00:20:15,562 --> 00:20:18,332
back then is coming back to me.

492
00:20:19,902 --> 00:20:22,842
(Pondering)

493
00:20:23,912 --> 00:20:25,142
It's coming back.

494
00:20:27,442 --> 00:20:31,612
In my opinion, being a manga artist...

495
00:20:31,852 --> 00:20:32,912
is...

496
00:20:33,712 --> 00:20:34,721
It's the most...

497
00:20:34,722 --> 00:20:35,751
difficult.

498
00:20:35,752 --> 00:20:36,882
- Difficult. - Difficult.

499
00:20:39,622 --> 00:20:42,092
Is being a manga artist difficult for you as well?

500
00:20:44,092 --> 00:20:47,092
The occupation suits me.

501
00:20:47,232 --> 00:20:49,332
- It isn't easy to say that. - It's hard.

502
00:20:49,862 --> 00:20:51,372
It really suits him.

503
00:20:51,902 --> 00:20:52,932
Really?

504
00:20:53,832 --> 00:20:57,812
He really seemed like a master.

505
00:20:58,612 --> 00:21:00,312
He seemed like a proper manga artist.

506
00:21:02,112 --> 00:21:03,412
He's incredible.

507
00:21:03,812 --> 00:21:07,782
I wanted to be like him.

508
00:21:08,582 --> 00:21:11,622
I wanted to draw comics like him.

509
00:21:14,122 --> 00:21:18,032
(As he drew comics for many years,)

510
00:21:19,462 --> 00:21:23,032
(he dreamed of how he'd be in the future every night.)

511
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:25,172
What I've drawn...

512
00:21:25,572 --> 00:21:29,372
(I wanted to be like Ito Junji.)

513
00:21:31,342 --> 00:21:34,982
(My idol seemed close, but also out of reach.)

514
00:21:36,242 --> 00:21:37,751
I never reached that level.

515
00:21:37,752 --> 00:21:39,352
I can only stare at it.

516
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:43,322
I've always thought that athletes...

517
00:21:44,122 --> 00:21:46,822
such as soccer players and MMA fighters were very cool.

518
00:21:47,722 --> 00:21:51,591
I realized that a manga artist could be even cooler.

519
00:21:51,592 --> 00:21:53,891
(I realized that a manga artist could be even cooler.)

520
00:21:53,892 --> 00:21:55,032
I was jealous too.

521
00:21:55,432 --> 00:21:56,731
You're the same.

522
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:57,732
- Exactly. - That's right.

523
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:00,841
But I was looking at him as someone who never reached...

524
00:22:00,842 --> 00:22:02,472
that level.

525
00:22:02,772 --> 00:22:04,811
It felt a bit strange, to be honest.

526
00:22:04,812 --> 00:22:06,542
You know,

527
00:22:06,672 --> 00:22:09,341
everyone hits a roadblock in life.

528
00:22:09,342 --> 00:22:11,852
But someone else might clear it for you.

529
00:22:12,212 --> 00:22:15,851
Mr. Ito Junji might clear it for you through this opportunity.

530
00:22:15,852 --> 00:22:17,121
I should keep my options open.

531
00:22:17,122 --> 00:22:18,751
You might want to draw comics again.

532
00:22:18,752 --> 00:22:19,821
