- You can see the Ferris wheel. - You're right.

802
00:34:41,632 --> 00:34:43,332
They're having fireworks!

803
00:34:43,832 --> 00:34:45,032
They're having fireworks!

804
00:34:46,032 --> 00:34:47,502
Perfect timing.

805
00:34:50,772 --> 00:34:52,541
- Is that Disneyland? - That's Disneyland.

806
00:34:52,542 --> 00:34:54,912
(They see the fireworks from the theme park near the house.)

807
00:34:55,312 --> 00:34:56,441
Do they have fireworks every day?

808
00:34:56,442 --> 00:34:58,312
They have fireworks every day at this hour. Isn't it nice?

809
00:34:58,412 --> 00:34:59,452
Yes.

810
00:35:02,622 --> 00:35:05,522
(Looking at the fireworks reminds him of someone.)

811
00:35:07,852 --> 00:35:11,492
(Meeting with his idol was as intense as fireworks.)

812
00:35:16,262 --> 00:35:20,932
(He stares at the fireworks quietly as he thinks about the moment.)

813
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:22,242
It's nice.

814
00:35:25,242 --> 00:35:26,511
(They wake up from the dream and come back inside.)

815
00:35:26,512 --> 00:35:27,512
It's a nice house.

816
00:35:28,242 --> 00:35:29,942
- It's warm inside, right? - Yes.

817
00:35:30,482 --> 00:35:31,582
It's nice.

818
00:35:32,282 --> 00:35:33,711
(Let's see.)

819
00:35:33,712 --> 00:35:35,851
Did your father bring these liquors?

820
00:35:35,852 --> 00:35:37,851
- My dad can't drink. - Okay.

821
00:35:37,852 --> 00:35:38,992
So he collected liquors instead.

822
00:35:41,292 --> 00:35:42,992
This liquor was made in Seoul in 1988.

823
00:35:43,322 --> 00:35:45,262
Gosh, for the Summer Games at Seoul.

824
00:35:45,362 --> 00:35:46,391
- There were many cool liquors. - Is it...

825
00:35:46,392 --> 00:35:48,032
- from 1988? - Yes.

826
00:35:48,332 --> 00:35:49,932
Is it Coke?

827
00:35:50,132 --> 00:35:51,972
- It's from 1981. - Coke from 1981.

828
00:35:52,732 --> 00:35:53,932
There are many precious items.

829
00:35:55,142 --> 00:35:57,372
That's from 1984. Golf.

830
00:35:58,572 --> 00:35:59,911
He likes baseball and golf.

831
00:35:59,912 --> 00:36:01,942
(The collection has liquors from each era.)

832
00:36:02,282 --> 00:36:03,382
Do you want to see my room?

833
00:36:04,642 --> 00:36:05,752
It's to the left.

834
00:36:09,122 --> 00:36:10,281
I grew up here...

835
00:36:10,282 --> 00:36:11,852
- since the age of three. - Since you were a baby.

836
00:36:11,992 --> 00:36:13,352
Yes. I used this room since the age of three.

837
00:36:13,752 --> 00:36:15,591
(The room holds traces of him from his childhood to now.)

838
00:36:15,592 --> 00:36:16,662
This is your room.

839
00:36:19,462 --> 00:36:23,062
It's from the time Mom hit the door with a frying pan.

840
00:36:23,262 --> 00:36:24,702
- Here. - Why did she do that?

841
00:36:24,972 --> 00:36:26,602
She was angry. She wanted me to open the door.

842
00:36:27,002 --> 00:36:28,471
Did you lock yourself inside?

843
00:36:28,472 --> 00:36:30,141
- My mom was angry, - Okay.

844
00:36:30,142 --> 00:36:31,942
- so I shut the door. - You did that.

845
00:36:32,312 --> 00:36:35,212
So she hit the door with a frying pan.

846
00:36:35,782 --> 00:36:38,982
- Let's say her son ran away. - Okay.

847
00:36:39,582 --> 00:36:41,051
- And he locked the door. - Okay.

848
00:36:41,052 --> 00:36:42,551
My mom could create...

849
00:36:42,552 --> 00:36:45,122
a situation in which her son had to open the door.

850
00:36:45,722 --> 00:36:47,392
What did she do? Can you guess?

851
00:36:48,162 --> 00:36:49,622
What? What did she do?

852
00:36:51,076 --> 00:36:52,445
My mom could create...

853
00:36:52,446 --> 00:36:55,016
a situation in which her son had to open the door.

854
00:36:55,586 --> 00:36:57,185
- What did she do? - What? What did she do?

855
00:36:57,186 --> 00:36:58,226
Look at the structure.

856
00:36:59,626 --> 00:37:00,686
- What? - What?

857
00:37:01,156 --> 00:37:02,326
- What did she do? - What did she do?

858
00:37:02,696 --> 00:37:05,026
- The room is below the hole. - Right.

859
00:37:05,496 --> 00:37:06,995
What do you think will happen if she keeps adding water?

860
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:07,996
- It'll get flooded. - Gosh.

861
00:37:08,236 --> 00:37:10,265
- Did she pour water? - She poured water...

862
00:37:10,266 --> 00:37:12,166
- until I opened the door. - Really?

863
00:37:12,336 --> 00:37:15,136
When the room got flooded, I had to open the door.

864
00:37:15,706 --> 00:37:17,205
Just what did you do?

865
00:37:17,206 --> 00:37:19,576
I don't remember. But my mom was very angry.

866
00:37:19,906 --> 00:37:21,676
- I guess it was something big. - Right.

867
00:37:21,946 --> 00:37:23,045
Didn't you see it?

868
00:37:23,046 --> 00:37:24,476
There's a dented frying pan.

869
00:37:25,116 --> 00:37:27,016
It got dented when she hit Kangnam with it.

870
00:37:27,786 --> 00:37:30,656
- He showed me that. - Kangnam really is a strong man.

871
00:37:31,156 --> 00:37:33,026
- Is that why he's called Kangnam? - It stands for "A strong man."

872
00:37:33,186 --> 00:37:34,356
- She raised him as a strong man. - Really?

873
00:37:35,126 --> 00:37:36,256
It was dented like this.

874
00:37:37,456 --> 00:37:38,495
My mom is a genius.

875
00:37:38,496 --> 00:37:40,095
(Laughing)

876
00:37:40,096 --> 00:37:42,336
Thank goodness the wood didn't go bad.

877
00:37:42,836 --> 00:37:44,195
They had to replace the wood.

878
00:37:44,196 --> 00:37:45,436
(They had to replace the wood.)

879
00:37:46,566 --> 00:37:49,206
(Kangnam begins to prepare dinner.)

880
00:37:50,136 --> 00:37:52,506
(Meanwhile, Kian84 takes off the jacket.)

881
00:37:54,576 --> 00:37:58,686
(He goes to the sink.)

882
00:38:05,086 --> 00:38:08,256
(He washes the empty container that held lunch for his idol.)

883
00:38:11,556 --> 00:38:13,266
Mr. Ito Junji...

884
00:38:14,026 --> 00:38:15,266
- ate everything. - He ate everything.

885
00:38:15,396 --> 00:38:16,736
I'm so touched.

886
00:38:17,096 --> 00:38:18,196
I'm so touched.

887
00:38:18,306 --> 00:38:21,536
- Did he eat all the food? - He didn't leave anything.

888
00:38:24,006 --> 00:38:26,906
(He reminisces upon what happened as he looks at the container.)

889
00:38:29,746 --> 00:38:35,356
(Kangnam begins to cook in earnest.)

890
00:38:36,686 --> 00:38:38,386
It doesn't look half bad.

891
00:38:39,356 --> 00:38:41,485
(Kangnam's sukiyaki is ready in no time.)

892
00:38:41,486 --> 00:38:43,726
- It looks tasty. - It looks so delicious.

893
00:38:44,696 --> 00:38:45,995
- Cheers. - Cheers.

894
00:38:45,996 --> 00:38:47,965
Thank you for your hard work.

895
00:38:47,966 --> 00:38:49,095
- Thank you for your hard work. - Well done.

896
00:38:49,096 --> 00:38:50,636
(Thank you for your hard work.)

897
00:38:51,036 --> 00:38:53,406
(Drinking)

898
00:38:55,236 --> 00:38:56,236
(My goodness)

899
00:38:57,736 --> 00:38:58,746
(Gosh)

900
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:03,046
Try it. Try the meat first.

901
00:39:04,776 --> 00:39:06,386
- Thank you for the food. - Okay.

902
00:39:07,616 --> 00:39:10,985
In Japan, they serve sukiyaki to an important guest.

903
00:39:10,986 --> 00:39:12,056
I see.

904
00:39:12,386 --> 00:39:14,726
Dip it... Dip it in the egg mixture.

905
00:39:15,256 --> 00:39:16,356
I did that.

906
00:39:17,656 --> 00:39:19,265
(Let me try it as well.)

907
00:39:19,266 --> 00:39:21,326
- Hey, you didn't add any water. - No.

908
00:39:22,036 --> 00:39:23,066
But it isn't salty.

909
00:39:24,136 --> 00:39:25,205
(The taste makes him nod.)

910
00:39:25,206 --> 00:39:26,466
Of course, it's delicious.

911
00:39:27,136 --> 00:39:28,976
- It's good, right? - It's good.

912
00:39:29,476 --> 00:39:30,806
- Not bad, right? - It's good.

913
00:39:32,676 --> 00:39:33,876
(He picks up some konjac jelly noodles.)

914
00:39:33,976 --> 00:39:35,945
Konjac jelly noodles taste really good to me.

915
00:39:35,946 --> 00:39:38,585
The konjac jelly was good. It tasted good like that.

916
00:39:38,586 --> 00:39:40,146
- Right - Drenched in the sauce.

917
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:43,386
- There's a lot of tofu. - Right.

918
00:39:45,186 --> 00:39:48,796
(It's his first proper meal in Japan.)

919
00:39:50,356 --> 00:39:54,366
(Kangnam shoves down the plain rice.)

920
00:39:54,666 --> 00:39:56,095
This is the happiest moment.

921
00:39:56,096 --> 00:39:58,096
(This is the happiest moment.)

922
00:39:58,836 --> 00:40:01,506
(He takes a big bite of happiness.)

923
00:40:02,576 --> 00:40:05,576
It feels like I owe you one.

924
00:40:05,776 --> 00:40:06,876
Why think that way?

925
00:40:07,846 --> 00:40:11,346
I'll grant you a wish of whatever you want.

926
00:40:11,376 --> 00:40:12,746
- Really? - Yes.

927
00:40:14,286 --> 00:40:17,186
It's a really hard thing to be able to meet Mr. Ito Junji.

928
00:40:18,756 --> 00:40:19,926
You made it happen.

929
00:40:21,456 --> 00:40:22,456
Don't mention it.

930
00:40:23,226 --> 00:40:26,296
He seemed to respect you.

931
00:40:26,866 --> 00:40:28,025
Why would he respect me?

932
00:40:28,026 --> 00:40:30,066
He checked your work after I contacted him.

933
00:40:30,466 --> 00:40:32,136
He agreed to meet you after that.

934
00:40:32,436 --> 00:40:34,206
(Really?)

935
00:40:34,606 --> 00:40:36,676
That's a great honor.

936
00:40:38,076 --> 00:40:41,176
It felt like meeting a superstar.

937
00:40:42,376 --> 00:40:43,946
He was small in size,

938
00:40:44,416 --> 00:40:45,686
but he seemed really big to me.

939
00:40:47,946 --> 00:40:50,656
It was my first time meeting an artist as well.

940
00:40:50,856 --> 00:40:53,286
I had no chance to meet an animation artist.

941
00:40:53,826 --> 00:40:55,396
- As he works in a different field. - Right.

942
00:40:55,796 --> 00:40:58,026
It was great as he was very pleasant with us.

943
00:40:58,426 --> 00:40:59,896
- Right. - Right.

944
00:41:01,596 --> 00:41:04,796
I wonder if he will want to see me in Korea next time.

945
00:41:05,536 --> 00:41:07,505
I talked with him a bit...

946
00:41:07,506 --> 00:41:09,736
- when you were away. - Right.

947
00:41:10,106 --> 00:41:14,845
I think he has plans to visit Korea with his family.

948
00:41:14,846 --> 00:41:18,046
- In case he really comes, - Right.

949
00:41:18,686 --> 00:41:20,146
- I should work on my Japanese. - Right.

950
00:41:20,616 --> 00:41:23,456
I feel like I'm gaining momentum.

951
00:41:23,756 --> 00:41:25,285
- Is that so? - Right.

952
00:41:25,286 --> 00:41:26,786
I enjoy it.

953
00:41:27,086 --> 00:41:28,855
I enjoy it like the first time...

954
00:41:28,856 --> 00:41:31,326
- I started running last year. - Right.

955
00:41:31,696 --> 00:41:34,196
Studying is fun.

956
00:41:35,126 --> 00:41:37,166
I never thought studying was something fun in my life.

957
00:41:37,496 --> 00:41:38,606
It never happened before?

958
00:41:38,706 --> 00:41:41,765
Studying was something I've always hated.

959
00:41:41,766 --> 00:41:43,676
But this is fun for some reason.

960
00:41:43,906 --> 00:41:45,145
- Gosh. - It's weird.

961
00:41:45,146 --> 00:41:46,705
It must feel fun as you have purpose behind it.

962
00:41:46,706 --> 00:41:48,515
- Right. - This will make things faster.

963
00:41:48,516 --> 00:41:49,975
- It's fun. - There will be even more momentum.

964
00:41:49,976 --> 00:41:51,646
- Right. - It isn't fun if it's forced.

965
00:41:53,646 --> 00:41:54,816
How was today?

966
00:41:55,916 --> 00:41:56,986
Today,

967
00:41:58,526 --> 00:42:01,386
thanks to Mr. Ito Junji,

968
00:42:01,856 --> 00:42:04,295
- Gosh. - You know how to say "thanks to?"

969
00:42:04,296 --> 00:42:05,565
You know how to say "thanks to?"

970
00:42:05,566 --> 00:42:07,365
- Of course. - Look at you.

971
00:42:07,366 --> 00:42:08,836
Gosh, Kian84!

972
00:42:08,996 --> 00:42:10,665
That's a difficult term.

973
00:42:10,666 --> 00:42:11,795
Right. Not a lot of people know that one.

974
00:42:11,796 --> 00:42:13,706
- Beginners don't know that one. - Right.

975
00:42:14,606 --> 00:42:17,476
Thanks to Mr. Ito Junji,

976
00:42:19,306 --> 00:42:22,446
I studied Japanese...

977
00:42:22,746 --> 00:42:25,416
for the first time.

978
00:42:25,786 --> 00:42:27,146
And...

979
00:42:27,946 --> 00:42:29,856
thanks to you,

980
00:42:30,056 --> 00:42:31,356
it feels like...

981
00:42:33,126 --> 00:42:34,726
I found...

982
00:42:36,196 --> 00:42:38,396
a new life.

983
00:42:38,866 --> 00:42:41,626
Your Japanese is good all of a sudden with some alcohol.

984
00:42:44,096 --> 00:42:46,035
- That's natural. - Right.

985
00:42:46,036 --> 00:42:47,465
- That happens naturally. - It pops out.

986
00:42:47,466 --> 00:42:49,305
It's your doubt inside you that always stops you.

987
00:42:49,306 --> 00:42:50,975
- Right. - There's no shame.

988
00:42:50,976 --> 00:42:52,406
- It just comes out boldly. - Right.

989
00:42:53,946 --> 00:42:55,176
So...

990
00:42:56,376 --> 00:42:58,476
toward you, I really...

991
00:42:59,386 --> 00:43:01,216
- and seriously... - He's saying it boldly.

992
00:43:02,186 --> 00:43:03,456
feel thankful.

993
00:43:04,616 --> 00:43:06,656
I have that heart toward you.

994
00:43:10,196 --> 00:43:14,425
When you read Ito Junji's comics,

995
00:43:14,426 --> 00:43:16,136
there's a certain feeling.

996
00:43:17,796 --> 00:43:20,936
There are scary ones, but there are ones...

997
00:43:21,536 --> 00:43:26,006
that make you feel like...

998
00:43:26,206 --> 00:43:28,206
you've had a strange dream.

999
00:43:29,676 --> 00:43:32,485
It felt like I was part of one of his comics today.

1000
00:43:32,486 --> 00:43:35,485
Unimaginable things happened.

1001
00:43:35,486 --> 00:43:40,986
(The idol he has always dreamed of)

1002
00:43:41,786 --> 00:43:45,866
(Spending time with Mr. Ito Junji)

1003
00:43:47,226 --> 00:43:49,866
(It was a thrilling day he will never forget about.)

1004
00:43:50,636 --> 00:43:52,206
It feels like...

1005
00:43:54,106 --> 00:43:56,236
I'm in a strange dream.

1006
00:43:57,836 --> 00:44:02,576
To me, he is like the universe.

1007
00:44:02,776 --> 00:44:04,645
(Finally Encountering My Universe)

1008
00:44:04,646 --> 00:44:05,746
Impressive.

1009
00:44:07,416 --> 00:44:09,455
The first guest of the Running Horses Special.

1010
00:44:09,456 --> 00:44:12,355
Bae Na Ra is here. Welcome!

1011
00:44:12,356 --> 00:44:13,426
- Hello. - Born in the Year of the Horse.

1012
00:44:14,326 --> 00:44:16,856
What was the response after being on the show?

1013
00:44:17,026 --> 00:44:20,966
Many people contacted me saying they enjoyed my episode.

1014
00:44:21,626 --> 00:44:23,766
(His day was full of consistent routines.)

1015
00:44:24,836 --> 00:44:26,505
(With his own rhythm,)

1016
00:44:26,506 --> 00:44:28,976
(the Routine Man lives each day.)

1017
00:44:29,236 --> 00:44:30,535
("I love his life with routine filled with neatness.")

1018
00:44:30,536 --> 00:44:31,736
("His life is so productive.")

1019
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:34,746
And I used the skating board.

1020
00:44:35,276 --> 00:44:36,316
(Sliding)

1021
00:44:36,376 --> 00:44:38,046
Many people said they bought it as well.

1022
00:44:38,716 --> 00:44:39,816
Really?

1023
00:44:40,046 --> 00:44:43,056
Through a DM on social media,

1024
00:44:43,086 --> 00:44:44,086
there was an owner who wanted to stop selling them...

1025
00:44:44,087 --> 00:44:45,456
- as business was bad. - Gosh!

1026
00:44:45,656 --> 00:44:47,956
The owner thanked me for helping out.

1027
00:44:48,796 --> 00:44:51,055
The Running Horses Special is feeling great.

1028
00:44:51,056 --> 00:44:53,565
I'm curious about what kind of day you've spent this time.

1029
00:44:53,566 --> 00:44:54,566
- Let's take a look. - Right.

1030
00:45:01,466 --> 00:45:04,436
(Na Ra's World)

1031
00:45:06,106 --> 00:45:10,516
(He's sleeping with his blanket over his face.)

1032
00:45:12,646 --> 00:45:13,646
(Struggling)

1033
00:45:15,216 --> 00:45:17,456
(Tossing and turning)

1034
00:45:19,026 --> 00:45:21,426
(He finally shows his face.)

1035
00:45:22,756 --> 00:45:24,026
Wait. He's not at home.

1036
00:45:24,556 --> 00:45:25,625
- It's a tent. - It's a tent.

1037
00:45:25,626 --> 00:45:27,125
(He wakes up in a tent.)

1038
00:45:27,126 --> 00:45:28,126
It's still cold outside.

1039
00:45:29,096 --> 00:45:31,366
I cover my eyes and ears.

1040
00:45:31,596 --> 00:45:33,206
Right. He slept with a sleep mask.

1041
00:45:33,536 --> 00:45:35,036
Right. He covered his whole face.

1042
00:45:35,436 --> 00:45:36,935
It makes me feel like I'm in the same place...

1043
00:45:36,936 --> 00:45:38,006
no matter where I am.

1044
00:45:39,276 --> 00:45:41,245
Do you feel the same way in there as well?

1045
00:45:41,246 --> 00:45:42,316
Gosh, it's hot.

1046
00:45:42,476 --> 00:45:43,615
The tent looks really nice.

1047
00:45:43,616 --> 00:45:45,246
The tent is really big.

1048
00:45:45,416 --> 00:45:46,616
He knows how to enjoy a camping trip.

1049
00:45:47,186 --> 00:45:48,855
- There's a heater. - Right.

1050
00:45:48,856 --> 00:45:51,156
It has been a week since my musical was over.

1051
00:45:51,216 --> 00:45:54,125
To reward myself for working hard,

1052
00:45:54,126 --> 00:45:57,126
I came on a camping trip.

1053
00:45:57,496 --> 00:46:00,496
I came yesterday. It's my second day here.

1054
00:46:00,766 --> 00:46:03,265
It feels like he was there for... Oh, it's his second day.

1055
00:46:03,266 --> 00:46:04,296
(The wild traces of yesterday)

1056
00:46:04,366 --> 00:46:06,565
I went there for 3 days and 2 nights.

1057
00:46:06,566 --> 00:46:09,235
You go camping for up to 3 days and 2 nights?

1058
00:46:09,236 --> 00:46:11,836
Yes. As the size of the tent is quite big,

1059
00:46:11,876 --> 00:46:13,375
installing the tent...

1060
