1318
00:56:25,956 --> 00:56:27,325
It was a salad sauce.

1319
00:56:27,326 --> 00:56:29,456
I made a simple cucumber salad.

1320
00:56:30,156 --> 00:56:32,256
(Eating)

1321
00:56:33,066 --> 00:56:34,296
(It tastes good as well.)

1322
00:56:35,196 --> 00:56:38,136
(The boiled doenjang jjigae is brought up.)

1323
00:56:39,836 --> 00:56:42,535
He does everything so naturally.

1324
00:56:42,536 --> 00:56:43,776
- It's done so smoothly. - Right.

1325
00:56:44,976 --> 00:56:46,946
(Focused)

1326
00:56:50,816 --> 00:56:51,915
The cooking torch?

1327
00:56:51,916 --> 00:56:53,086
(He even uses a cooking torch.)

1328
00:56:53,746 --> 00:56:54,786
(Picking up)

1329
00:56:58,056 --> 00:56:59,586
Why does the spice container look like that?

1330
00:56:59,656 --> 00:57:02,795
I made that spice container myself.

1331
00:57:02,796 --> 00:57:04,756
I went to a variety store.

1332
00:57:05,056 --> 00:57:06,895
And I bought several four-can containers,

1333
00:57:06,896 --> 00:57:08,726
and joined them together.

1334
00:57:08,926 --> 00:57:10,865
- You take them out when needed. - Right.

1335
00:57:10,866 --> 00:57:12,235
- Like this. - That's what I do.

1336
00:57:12,236 --> 00:57:13,236
That must be convenient.

1337
00:57:13,237 --> 00:57:14,705
How many kinds are there?

1338
00:57:14,706 --> 00:57:15,735
I have all sorts of things. Things like cumin,

1339
00:57:15,736 --> 00:57:17,575
shichimi, and bonito flakes.

1340
00:57:17,576 --> 00:57:18,876
(I have all sorts of things.)

1341
00:57:19,446 --> 00:57:20,546
Maldon Salt.

1342
00:57:20,846 --> 00:57:22,276
- Maldon Salt? - Right.

1343
00:57:22,476 --> 00:57:24,316
It's for the meat.

1344
00:57:24,716 --> 00:57:26,416
- I also have herb salt. - Herb salt?

1345
00:57:26,586 --> 00:57:28,346
- He has three types of salt. - As a seasoning.

1346
00:57:29,816 --> 00:57:33,286
(The first can of the spice container)

1347
00:57:33,986 --> 00:57:36,426
(Salt for grilled meat)

1348
00:57:37,856 --> 00:57:39,895
(He also sprinkles the pepper from the second can.)

1349
00:57:39,896 --> 00:57:40,925
They're all connected.

1350
00:57:40,926 --> 00:57:43,296
- They must be made that way. - Right.

1351
00:57:45,266 --> 00:57:47,906
I get excited on my own while getting things prepared.

1352
00:57:48,166 --> 00:57:50,506
- I imagine it in my head. - The things you like.

1353
00:57:51,676 --> 00:57:55,245
(He gets a generous amount of his favorite dish.)

1354
00:57:55,246 --> 00:57:57,376
(One more time)

1355
00:57:58,716 --> 00:58:04,156
(I must take a picture of this.)

1356
00:58:05,786 --> 00:58:08,525
(His meal looks flawless.)

1357
00:58:08,526 --> 00:58:10,356
(A perfect meal with the brisket)

1358
00:58:10,656 --> 00:58:14,496
Oyster bossam is a common dish when I go camping.

1359
00:58:14,726 --> 00:58:16,736
When there are leftover oysters,

1360
00:58:17,096 --> 00:58:19,235
I make oyster jeon with eggs.

1361
00:58:19,236 --> 00:58:20,336
That's the best thing to make.

1362
00:58:20,436 --> 00:58:23,636
And I also make spicy fishcake soup and kalguksu.

1363
00:58:23,876 --> 00:58:25,906
- I made gambas al ajillo as well. - He made everything possible.

1364
00:58:27,806 --> 00:58:30,476
I'm learning how to cook these days. We should go together some time.

1365
00:58:31,816 --> 00:58:33,015
- You are always welcome. - I'm learning how to cook.

1366
00:58:33,016 --> 00:58:34,286
I would love that.

1367
00:58:34,716 --> 00:58:37,555
I learn how to make around two dishes each time.

1368
00:58:37,556 --> 00:58:38,986
- At a cooking school? - Yes.

1369
00:58:39,186 --> 00:58:40,586
- You go to a cooking school? - You go to a cooking school?

1370
00:58:41,086 --> 00:58:42,155
Yes. A cooking school.

1371
00:58:42,156 --> 00:58:44,855
- That's fascinating. - As I've never tried cooking,

1372
00:58:44,856 --> 00:58:47,365
- I have no basic knowledge at all. - Gosh. You're committed.

1373
00:58:47,366 --> 00:58:49,125
As if it's personal training at a gym, I'm working hard to learn.

1374
00:58:49,126 --> 00:58:50,496
- That's a good idea. - Personal cooking.

1375
00:58:53,136 --> 00:58:54,636
Thank you for the meal.

1376
00:58:55,306 --> 00:58:56,306
All right.

1377
00:58:59,176 --> 00:59:00,745
(He slurps the soup first.)

1378
00:59:00,746 --> 00:59:01,946
That looks really good.

1379
00:59:02,176 --> 00:59:03,276
Gosh, this is great!

1380
00:59:06,886 --> 00:59:09,016
(Satisfied)

1381
00:59:11,886 --> 00:59:13,356
- That's all you need. - Right.

1382
00:59:13,756 --> 00:59:16,085
It tastes better when it gets boiled even more.

1383
00:59:16,086 --> 00:59:17,496
- Right. - Right.

1384
00:59:17,796 --> 00:59:19,525
All jjigaes taste better the second time.

1385
00:59:19,526 --> 00:59:20,866
- The 2nd and 3rd time. - Right.

1386
00:59:21,996 --> 00:59:25,036
(It tastes good from the first bite.)

1387
00:59:26,136 --> 00:59:28,466
(Sizzling)

1388
00:59:32,106 --> 00:59:34,605
(Having a piece of well-grilled meat as well)

1389
00:59:34,606 --> 00:59:35,676
It's way better.

1390
00:59:41,846 --> 00:59:43,855
(This time, he mixes rice with the stew.)

1391
00:59:43,856 --> 00:59:45,585
- Gosh, that's... - Gosh, while looking at the sea...

1392
00:59:45,586 --> 00:59:47,186
Doenjang jjigae and rice. That's the best.

1393
00:59:56,596 --> 00:59:59,766
(Having a bite of the cucumber salad)

1394
01:00:03,306 --> 01:00:04,706
(Glancing)

1395
01:00:06,176 --> 01:00:08,476
(He looks outside while eating.)

1396
01:00:11,246 --> 01:00:15,686
I try to enjoy nature as much as possible.

1397
01:00:16,516 --> 01:00:18,486
When I look outside,

1398
01:00:18,916 --> 01:00:22,056
I can hear the sea, birds, and wind.

1399
01:00:22,526 --> 01:00:25,056
Then I feel like I'm in nature.

1400
01:00:27,196 --> 01:00:30,596
(He enjoyed the morning with nature.)

1401
01:00:31,936 --> 01:00:34,336
(Nature-friendly dishwashing)

1402
01:00:41,276 --> 01:00:43,476
What do you think about when you eat alone?

1403
01:00:43,776 --> 01:00:45,475
Nothing comes to mind, really.

1404
01:00:45,476 --> 01:00:48,016
It's just nice.

1405
01:00:48,386 --> 01:00:50,656
I don't think about what to do next.

1406
01:00:50,886 --> 01:00:51,886
"I should do something."

1407
01:00:51,886 --> 01:00:52,886
- I don't worry about that. - You're not pressed.

1408
01:00:53,156 --> 01:00:54,625
- Right. I'm not pressed. - You go there to empty your mind.

1409
01:00:54,626 --> 01:00:55,656
That's right.

1410
01:00:57,626 --> 01:01:00,626
(While leisurely gazing at the sea,)

1411
01:01:03,166 --> 01:01:08,136
(he relaxedly wraps up the morning.)

1412
01:01:09,536 --> 01:01:10,676
Gosh, I'm so full.

1413
01:01:17,376 --> 01:01:18,946
(Putting it on)

1414
01:01:20,286 --> 01:01:23,786
(Na Ra heads somewhere after getting changed.)

1415
01:01:25,656 --> 01:01:27,225
There's a convenience store nearby.

1416
01:01:27,226 --> 01:01:29,456
- It's great. - Yes. There's a burger place too.

1417
01:01:30,056 --> 01:01:31,526
- There's a burger place too. - Fresh raw fish.

1418
01:01:33,166 --> 01:01:34,495
- That sounds good. - There's a raw fish restaurant too.

1419
01:01:34,496 --> 01:01:35,566
Yes.

1420
01:01:36,196 --> 01:01:37,296
Okay.

1421
01:01:39,836 --> 01:01:41,036
- Oh, he's running? - Right after eating?

1422
01:01:41,706 --> 01:01:43,275
- That's a mountain. - I'm running lightly.

1423
01:01:43,276 --> 01:01:44,276
(He starts running uphill.)

1424
01:01:44,277 --> 01:01:45,976
Gosh, it's uphill.

1425
01:01:46,376 --> 01:01:47,506
It's uphill.

1426
01:01:48,246 --> 01:01:50,116
It's great. It's even better.

1427
01:01:51,176 --> 01:01:54,846
(Na Ra ran whenever he had a chance.)

1428
01:01:56,046 --> 01:01:58,056
(He runs a lap even when he's camping.)

1429
01:01:59,656 --> 01:02:01,956
(Amazed)

1430
01:02:02,826 --> 01:02:04,056
Gosh, it's so nice.

1431
01:02:05,526 --> 01:02:07,066
Gosh, this place is pretty.

1432
01:02:08,326 --> 01:02:12,036
- Gosh, what is that? - His routine is the same as yours.

1433
01:02:12,166 --> 01:02:13,736
That's right. He enjoys a fun run.

1434
01:02:13,866 --> 01:02:16,636
- He likes running and camping. - That's right.

1435
01:02:17,406 --> 01:02:20,276
(Enjoying a happy run today as well)

1436
01:02:22,706 --> 01:02:24,346
Look at that. He's stopping.

1437
01:02:24,746 --> 01:02:28,546
I always do healthy running.

1438
01:02:28,786 --> 01:02:29,985
- Fun running? - You do fun running.

1439
01:02:29,986 --> 01:02:31,385
- He does fun running. - Come here.

1440
01:02:31,386 --> 01:02:32,485
- He does fun running. - There you go.

1441
01:02:32,486 --> 01:02:34,926
I was being careful not to touch your hand.

1442
01:02:35,386 --> 01:02:37,925
You still haven't given up on fun running.

1443
01:02:37,926 --> 01:02:39,695
I saw a marathon recently, and there were a lot of people.

1444
01:02:39,696 --> 01:02:41,025
There were a lot.

1445
01:02:41,026 --> 01:02:42,596
I think I still need to work on it more.

1446
01:02:42,926 --> 01:02:44,836
Why would you decide that based on the atmosphere?

1447
01:02:46,036 --> 01:02:48,966
It's gotten warmer, so more people are running.

1448
01:02:49,366 --> 01:02:50,805
- It's about time you step up. - I tried killing the trend,

1449
01:02:50,806 --> 01:02:51,806
but it keeps coming back.

1450
01:02:51,807 --> 01:02:52,936
There are too many people.

1451
01:02:54,206 --> 01:02:55,246
Well...

1452
01:02:58,416 --> 01:02:59,446
What?

1453
01:02:59,616 --> 01:03:00,686
What is it?

1454
01:03:01,816 --> 01:03:02,986
There's nothing much.

1455
01:03:03,316 --> 01:03:04,486
He must be looking for something.

1456
01:03:05,686 --> 01:03:07,186
Hello, ma'am.

1457
01:03:08,256 --> 01:03:09,726
I have something to ask.

1458
01:03:10,256 --> 01:03:12,396
Do you sell webfoot octopus?

1459
01:03:12,526 --> 01:03:14,066
Oh, webfoot octopus?

1460
01:03:14,726 --> 01:03:16,696
I ran today as well.

1461
01:03:17,236 --> 01:03:18,496
I saw a map,

1462
01:03:19,366 --> 01:03:21,436
and there was a port nearby.

1463
01:03:21,836 --> 01:03:25,976
Webfoot octopus is in season in March.

1464
01:03:27,046 --> 01:03:29,446
If you get a webfoot octopus full of roe...

1465
01:03:29,946 --> 01:03:32,575
and wrap it in a foil,

1466
01:03:32,576 --> 01:03:35,115
then put it on a charcoal grill with mayonnaise on,

1467
01:03:35,116 --> 01:03:37,216
it'll be incredibly savory.

1468
01:03:37,786 --> 01:03:39,016
I imagined that...

1469
01:03:40,326 --> 01:03:41,686
as I ran to the restaurant.

1470
01:03:42,156 --> 01:03:44,556
- It's the best in March and April. - It's really savory.

1471
01:03:44,756 --> 01:03:47,366
- Yes. - Do you sell webfoot octopus?

1472
01:03:47,666 --> 01:03:49,796
Do you sell webfoot octopus?

1473
01:03:50,666 --> 01:03:52,666
(Webfoot octopus at its peak season)

1474
01:03:53,606 --> 01:03:55,336
(The flesh is plump and chewy.)

1475
01:03:56,306 --> 01:03:58,135
(Do you have webfoot octopus that I love?)

1476
01:03:58,136 --> 01:03:59,906
- We don't have it yet. - You don't sell it?

1477
01:04:00,346 --> 01:04:01,375
You don't sell it?

1478
01:04:01,376 --> 01:04:02,905
- This is... - It is in season,

1479
01:04:02,906 --> 01:04:04,416
but I bet they don't sell it yet.

1480
01:04:04,816 --> 01:04:06,746
You don't have it yet? When do you sell it?

1481
01:04:07,786 --> 01:04:09,016
The boat has to go out to catch it.

1482
01:04:09,146 --> 01:04:10,915
- The boat has to go out? - It's still cold, so...

1483
01:04:10,916 --> 01:04:12,415
If you want to buy seafood,

1484
01:04:12,416 --> 01:04:13,886
you need to go to Oepori Seafood Market.

1485
01:04:13,986 --> 01:04:15,256
- What? - You need to cross the bridge.

1486
01:04:16,026 --> 01:04:18,296
It's a 15-minute drive, right?

1487
01:04:18,456 --> 01:04:19,596
- Yes. - By car, right?

1488
01:04:20,266 --> 01:04:21,725
(I see.)

1489
01:04:21,726 --> 01:04:23,366
All right. Thank you.

1490
01:04:23,766 --> 01:04:24,936
Then you need to run again.

1491
01:04:25,396 --> 01:04:27,565
If it's a 15-minute drive, fun runners don't run.

1492
01:04:27,566 --> 01:04:28,566
Exactly.

1493
01:04:29,166 --> 01:04:30,436
They don't have it either.

1494
01:04:32,706 --> 01:04:36,676
(He goes straight to the raw fish restaurant next to it.)

1495
01:04:37,016 --> 01:04:38,476
Hello, ma'am.

1496
01:04:38,846 --> 01:04:41,846
What kind of seafood do you sell?

1497
01:04:42,316 --> 01:04:43,355
We have sea bass, rockfish,

1498
01:04:43,356 --> 01:04:44,416
- Sea bass... - and flatfish.

1499
01:04:44,616 --> 01:04:46,656
- Sea bass, rockfish, and flatfish? - Yes.

1500
01:04:46,826 --> 01:04:49,686
Try going to Oepori Seafood Market.

1501
01:04:49,956 --> 01:04:51,425
- Oepori? - If you go there...

1502
01:04:51,426 --> 01:04:52,755
- You should go there. - Everyone told me...

1503
01:04:52,756 --> 01:04:54,126
- to go to Oepori Seafood Market. - Oh, really?

1504
01:04:54,666 --> 01:04:56,026
All right. Thank you!

1505
01:04:56,496 --> 01:04:57,566
Oepori?

1506
01:05:01,536 --> 01:05:02,605
Hold on.

1507
01:05:02,606 --> 01:05:03,806
(That wasn't my plan.)

1508
01:05:04,806 --> 01:05:07,245
It's a big market, so I need to go to another island.

1509
01:05:07,246 --> 01:05:08,275
(He thinks for a second as he has to go to another island.)

1510
01:05:08,276 --> 01:05:09,375
You can't.

1511
01:05:09,376 --> 01:05:10,546
(He thinks for a second as he has to go to another island.)

1512
01:05:10,716 --> 01:05:12,416
It looks like he must eat webfoot octopus.

1513
01:05:12,646 --> 01:05:15,145
- That's the thing about planners. - That's right.

1514
01:05:15,146 --> 01:05:16,445
That's the problem of Type J.

1515
01:05:16,446 --> 01:05:18,655
- You can have rockfish instead. - I'd change my plan right away.

1516
01:05:18,656 --> 01:05:20,656
If that's the case, I wouldn't go camping.

1517
01:05:20,856 --> 01:05:21,925
That's right.

1518
01:05:21,926 --> 01:05:24,425
If I crave webfoot octopus that much, I'd take a taxi...

1519
01:05:24,426 --> 01:05:25,955
to Oepori Seafood Market and eat it there.

1520
01:05:25,956 --> 01:05:27,665
- When you're camping? - Of course.

1521
01:05:27,666 --> 01:05:29,865
- You'd eat at the restaurant? - What's wrong with that?

1522
01:05:29,866 --> 01:05:30,866
As long as you have a webfoot octopus.

1523
01:05:30,867 --> 01:05:32,196
"What's wrong with that?"

1524
01:05:33,336 --> 01:05:34,765
No, then you'd ruin it.

1525
01:05:34,766 --> 01:05:36,366
If you eat at a restaurant,

1526
01:05:36,806 --> 01:05:37,835
- my plan for camping disappears. - Exactly.

1527
01:05:37,836 --> 01:05:39,775
- That's right. - There's no point of camping.

1528
01:05:39,776 --> 01:05:42,746
Like I said, I'd eat webfoot octopus at the market.

1529
01:05:43,006 --> 01:05:44,676
- Yes, that's the strange part. - How is it strange?

1530
01:05:44,776 --> 01:05:46,915
You are camping with the tent set up,

1531
01:05:46,916 --> 01:05:49,485
and you eat at a restaurant. Isn't that strange?

1532
01:05:49,486 --> 01:05:50,656
Isn't it fun?

1533
01:05:52,056 --> 01:05:53,356
You have to eat the roe.

1534
01:05:54,956 --> 01:05:56,026
Then...

1535
01:05:58,456 --> 01:06:01,866
Gosh, I should try going elsewhere.

1536
01:06:03,366 --> 01:06:04,835
(Searching for a seafood market nearby)

1537
01:06:04,836 --> 01:06:06,865
I'm trying to look up...

1538
01:06:06,866 --> 01:06:08,766
a nearby port.

1539
01:06:09,536 --> 01:06:11,036
What is Eoryujeong Port?

1540
01:06:13,376 --> 01:06:16,716
What kind of place is Eoryujeong Port?

1541
01:06:17,546 --> 01:06:20,645
Eoryujeong Port is a small port...

1542
01:06:20,646 --> 01:06:22,345
on Seokmo Island, one of the islands in Ganghwa Island.

1543
01:06:22,346 --> 01:06:25,816
You can buy seafood at Eoryujeong Port.

1544
01:06:26,256 --> 01:06:27,326
Especially...

1545
01:06:27,856 --> 01:06:30,196
You can buy seafood at Eoryujeong Port. Especially...

1546
01:06:30,396 --> 01:06:31,455
He's running.

1547
01:06:31,456 --> 01:06:32,556
(He stops the AI from talking and rushes there.)

1548
01:06:33,366 --> 01:06:34,496
- He's running there? - He's going there?

1549
01:06:34,596 --> 01:06:36,296
- Was it nearby? - It must've been nearby.

1550
01:06:36,836 --> 01:06:39,096
All right.

1551
01:06:39,596 --> 01:06:41,705
- It's 2.4km. - It's 2.4km?

1552
01:06:41,706 --> 01:06:43,676
- Running 2.4km isn't bad. - But it's uphill.

1553
01:06:43,906 --> 01:06:44,906
(Exhaling)

1554
01:06:45,576 --> 01:06:47,946
(Lightly running with joy)

1555
01:06:48,606 --> 01:06:49,775
Since I'm a runner...

1556
01:06:49,776 --> 01:06:51,275
That isn't a fun run.

1557
01:06:51,276 --> 01:06:52,876
He runs the slope like that? Goodness.

1558
01:06:54,546 --> 01:06:55,645
I'm coming.

1559
01:06:55,646 --> 01:06:59,915
(Let's run toward webfoot octopus that's in season.)

1560
01:06:59,916 --> 01:07:02,725
The webfoot octopus you eat after running like that...

1561
01:07:02,726 --> 01:07:04,256
- is even more delicious. - That's right.

1562
01:07:04,556 --> 01:07:07,595
It doesn't taste the same if you go to a restaurant in a taxi.

1563
01:07:07,596 --> 01:07:08,866
You need to eat it after some effort.

1564
01:07:09,066 --> 01:07:10,736
- I think I'd lose my appetite. - You need to run.

1565
01:07:11,296 --> 01:07:12,695
Why would you lose your appetite?

1566
01:07:12,696 --> 01:07:14,236
It's the best after a taxi ride.

1567
01:07:15,266 --> 01:07:17,805
(He runs so that he can enjoy webfoot octopus even more.)

1568
01:07:17,806 --> 01:07:20,276
Wait a minute. I have to go down again?

1569
01:07:23,046 --> 01:07:24,315
Gosh, this isn't easy.

1570
01:07:24,316 --> 01:07:25,676
(The way to see webfoot octopus isn't easy.)

1571
01:07:26,446 --> 01:07:27,746
All right. Let's run.

1572
01:07:28,686 --> 01:07:30,056
Great. It's even better.

1573
01:07:30,856 --> 01:07:32,016
It's even better.

1574
01:07:36,156 --> 01:07:37,555
His legs are long, so he's fast.

1575
01:07:37,556 --> 01:07:38,696
Of course, he's fast.

1576
01:07:41,426 --> 01:07:42,566
Is it here?

1577
01:07:43,296 --> 01:07:45,235
(To be continued)

1578
01:07:45,236 --> 01:07:46,266
No way.

1579
01:07:47,236 --> 01:07:49,036
- For real? - Did you go to the wrong place?

1580
01:07:49,712 --> 01:07:51,381
(Na Ra kept running to eat webfoot octopus.)

1581
01:07:51,382 --> 01:07:52,442
Is it here?

1582
01:07:55,112 --> 01:07:56,182
No way.

1583
01:07:57,152 --> 01:07:58,882
- For real? - Did you go to the wrong place?

1584
01:07:59,322 --> 01:08:00,951
- Are you serious? - What is it?

1585
01:08:00,952 --> 01:08:02,092
- What is that? - What?

1586
01:08:02,592 --> 01:08:04,061
- You need to go there? - Oh, you have to cross that?

1587
01:08:04,062 --> 01:08:05,092
(It's a mountain trail!)

1588
01:08:05,222 --> 01:08:06,291
How does the GPS guide you...

1589
01:08:06,292 --> 01:08:07,331
- to a mountain trail? - Exactly.

1590
01:08:07,332 --> 01:08:08,962
The map showed a strange path.

1591
01:08:09,332 --> 01:08:10,962
- Serves you right. - It didn't show a proper road.

1592
01:08:11,602 --> 01:08:12,802
"Serves you right?"

1593
01:08:13,002 --> 01:08:14,402
You didn't listen to me and didn't get on a taxi.

1594
01:08:14,972 --> 01:08:17,241
You're so childish.

1595
01:08:17,242 --> 01:08:18,242
(Super childish)

1596
01:08:18,672 --> 01:08:19,772
Is this the right way?

1597
01:08:20,212 --> 01:08:22,042
I don't think I can do trail running.

1598
01:08:23,442 --> 01:08:24,781
Is this really right?

1599
01:08:24,782 --> 01:08:26,212
(He begins running, feeling confused.)

1600
01:08:26,882 --> 01:08:28,081
(The path is becoming rougher.)

1601
01:08:28,082 --> 01:08:29,851
I just thought...

1602
01:08:29,852 --> 01:08:32,381
that it was a shortcut and kept running.

1603
01:08:32,382 --> 01:08:34,422
(He's only run for 600m so far.)

1604
01:08:34,852 --> 01:08:38,122
(A challenging journey toward webfoot octopus)

1605
01:08:38,322 --> 01:08:39,631
- Of course it's tiring. - It annoys you if you run...

1606
01:08:39,632 --> 01:08:40,661
in that padded jacket because it's hot.

1607
01:08:40,662 --> 01:08:41,692
That's right.

1608
01:08:41,832 --> 01:08:43,032
You stink of sweat, and it annoys you.

1609
01:08:44,632 --> 01:08:45,632
It's tiring.

1610
01:08:45,962 --> 01:08:46,972
Gosh, I'm tired.

1611
01:08:47,532 --> 01:08:48,602
I'm so tired.

1612
01:08:50,642 --> 01:08:51,642
It's tiring.

1613
01:08:51,643 --> 01:08:54,771
(This won't do. Let me take a break.)

1614
01:08:54,772 --> 01:08:55,812
It's so tiring.

1615
01:08:57,942 --> 01:08:59,011
Gosh, this is...

1616
01:08:59,012 --> 01:09:01,051
(Taking it off)

1617
01:09:01,052 --> 01:09:02,452
This never occurred to me.

1618
01:09:03,452 --> 01:09:06,392
(Let's run again.)

1619
01:09:07,552 --> 01:09:09,791
(On a long quest to find webfoot octopus...)

1620
01:09:09,792 --> 01:09:11,462
(that was part of his plan)

1621
01:09:11,962 --> 01:09:15,532
(Getting more and more out of breath)

1622
01:09:16,232 --> 01:09:18,731
(Am I there yet?)

1623
01:09:18,732 --> 01:09:20,331
I became lighter after taking off the padded jacket.

1624
01:09:20,332 --> 01:09:21,932
- That's right. - Right. And it's cooler.

1625
01:09:22,232 --> 01:09:23,272
- It's cooler. - Yes.

1626
01:09:25,242 --> 01:09:29,442
(He ran the mountain trail while panting.)

1627
01:09:30,982 --> 01:09:32,041
All right.

1628
01:09:32,042 --> 01:09:33,881
(Barking)

1629
01:09:33,882 --> 01:09:35,152
I'll leave.

1630
01:09:38,252 --> 01:09:39,282
Goodness.

1631
01:09:42,122 --> 01:09:43,162
What is that?

1632
01:09:43,822 --> 01:09:46,332
(Both the dog and birds root for Na Ra.)

1633
01:09:46,892 --> 01:09:47,931
Maintain a slow pace.

1634
01:09:47,932 --> 01:09:49,832
(Fueled by everyone's support)

1635
01:09:50,062 --> 01:09:52,131
All right. I'm almost there.

1636
01:09:52,132 --> 01:09:53,902
(He's almost done with the webfoot octopus march.)

1637
01:09:55,402 --> 01:09:56,542
I'm finally here.

1638
01:09:57,702 --> 01:10:00,412
(He ran 2.4km to meet...)

1639
01:10:02,342 --> 01:10:03,811
It's huge.

1640
01:10:03,812 --> 01:10:04,842
This place is nice.

1641
01:10:04,982 --> 01:10:06,012
It's here.

1642
01:10:06,652 --> 01:10:08,012
It was a little bigger than the other port.

1643
01:10:08,652 --> 01:10:11,181
(Entering right away to look for webfoot octopus)

1644
01:10:11,182 --> 01:10:12,482
- Hello, ma'am. - Hello.

1645
01:10:12,622 --> 01:10:14,851
Are these all the seafood you have?

1646
01:10:14,852 --> 01:10:15,891
Yes.

1647
01:10:15,892 --> 01:10:18,092
Abalone, sea cucumber,

1648
01:10:18,262 --> 01:10:19,991
sea squirt, oyster, clams...

1649
01:10:19,992 --> 01:10:21,432
It looks like they don't have webfoot octopus.

1650
01:10:21,592 --> 01:10:23,631
I guess webfoot octopus isn't available yet.

1651
01:10:23,632 --> 01:10:24,802
I guess they really don't have it.

1652
01:10:25,132 --> 01:10:26,161
It's not available yet?

1653
01:10:26,162 --> 01:10:28,672
It's available a little later than other places.

1654
01:10:29,372 --> 01:10:30,402
It's available a little later than other places.

1655
01:10:31,502 --> 01:10:32,772
It's available in May.

1656
01:10:33,312 --> 01:10:34,472
Oh, really?

1657
01:10:36,142 --> 01:10:38,511
(He overcame many obstacles...)

1658
01:10:38,512 --> 01:10:40,882
(to find webfoot octopus only.)

1659
01:10:41,382 --> 01:10:45,052
(He even came to the next village.)

1660
01:10:46,152 --> 01:10:48,292
(They don't have it either?)

1661
01:10:48,422 --> 01:10:50,761
What's the most delicious seafood among these?

1662
01:10:50,762 --> 01:10:52,562
We haven't started fishing operations yet.

1663
01:10:53,032 --> 01:10:54,062
Is that so?

1664
01:10:55,132 --> 01:10:57,432
Thank you. Have a good day.

1665
01:10:59,162 --> 01:11:02,632
(What do I do now?)

1666
01:11:06,672 --> 01:11:08,841
- He's running again? - He'll get a taxi in the end.

1667
01:11:08,842 --> 01:11:10,742
(Webfoot octopus, where on earth are you?)

1668
01:11:11,242 --> 01:11:13,651
(He found a direct seafood market.)

1669
01:11:13,652 --> 01:11:15,151
- Oh, a direct market. - I see.

1670
01:11:15,152 --> 01:11:17,021
- They must have it. - They must have it.

1671
01:11:17,022 --> 01:11:18,481
(Please)

1672
01:11:18,482 --> 01:11:19,522
No way.

1673
01:11:19,792 --> 01:11:21,752
(Clattering)

1674
01:11:22,452 --> 01:11:25,161
(It's closed.)

1675
01:11:25,162 --> 01:11:27,832
They must open only on weekends.

1676
01:11:29,732 --> 01:11:30,761
(Am I really not going to eat webfoot octopus?)

1677
01:11:30,762 --> 01:11:32,032
He must be frustrated.

1678
01:11:32,402 --> 01:11:34,502
I thought they'd have it for sure.

1679
01:11:34,872 --> 01:11:36,571
They said it wasn't the season to have webfoot octopus...

1680
01:11:36,572 --> 01:11:38,272
on Ganghwa Island yet.

1681
01:11:38,702 --> 01:11:42,411
So different regions have different seasons.

1682
01:11:42,412 --> 01:11:43,782
With that in mind,

1683
01:11:44,012 --> 01:11:47,882
I thought I should quickly come up with the next plan.

1684
01:11:48,982 --> 01:11:50,082
What do I do?

1685
01:11:52,122 --> 01:11:53,621
(Mental freeze)

1686
01:11:53,622 --> 01:11:55,722
- What do I do? - I had a mental breakdown then.

1687
01:11:56,092 --> 01:11:59,061
My plans for the day started falling apart.

1688
01:11:59,062 --> 01:12:00,461
Do you get stressed, then?

1689
01:12:00,462 --> 01:12:02,592
- That gives me stress. - Poor Type Js.

1690
01:12:05,302 --> 01:12:07,632
Hold on. A seafood market...

1691
01:12:08,402 --> 01:12:09,902
A seafood market in Oepo Port...

1692
01:12:11,472 --> 01:12:13,272
A direct seafood market? It's 7km away?

1693
01:12:14,572 --> 01:12:16,111
Gosh, seriously...

1694
01:12:16,112 --> 01:12:17,282
(I've already run 3.5km.)

1695
01:12:18,512 --> 01:12:20,511
That's too far to go all of a sudden.

1696
01:12:20,512 --> 01:12:22,511
Yes, he still has things to do when he gets back.

1697
01:12:22,512 --> 01:12:23,522
Right.

1698
01:12:24,952 --> 01:12:26,052
(Sighing)

1699
01:12:27,952 --> 01:12:30,721
(With just webfoot octopus on mind,)

1700
01:12:30,722 --> 01:12:34,362
(he continued to run.)

1701
01:12:40,402 --> 01:12:42,202
(Bitter)

1702
01:12:45,472 --> 01:12:46,871
I contemplated a lot.

1703
01:12:46,872 --> 01:12:48,011
(There's no webfoot octopus for me in this vast sea.)

1704
01:12:48,012 --> 01:12:50,342
That was totally meaningless.

1705
01:12:52,342 --> 01:12:54,582
It's just meaningless.

1706
01:12:55,052 --> 01:12:56,682
- We have a title. - Right.

1707
01:12:58,152 --> 01:13:00,992
(Title: "Meaningless")

1708
01:13:01,692 --> 01:13:03,921
(It's a bummer, but it can't be helped.)

1709
01:13:03,922 --> 01:13:05,362
(Acting fine)

1710
01:13:07,432 --> 01:13:09,492
(Clearing his throat)

1711
01:13:11,902 --> 01:13:12,962
Ma'am!

1712
01:13:14,072 --> 01:13:16,401
- Well, I... - What?

1713
01:13:16,402 --> 01:13:17,541
I wanted to cheer up.

1714
01:13:17,542 --> 01:13:18,542
- Is that so? - Yes.

1715
01:13:18,543 --> 01:13:21,242
I'll get some clams. What do you think?

1716
01:13:21,712 --> 01:13:23,181
We have scallops...

1717
01:13:23,182 --> 01:13:25,142
- They have many shellfish. - It's a spawning season.

1718
01:13:25,412 --> 01:13:27,051
Yes. I'll take 2kg.

1719
01:13:27,052 --> 01:13:28,212
- All right. - Okay.

1720
01:13:28,912 --> 01:13:30,121
Gosh, it looks delicious.

1721
01:13:30,122 --> 01:13:31,681
(His plan failed, but he replaced it with another seafood.)

1722
01:13:31,682 --> 01:13:34,152
I'll take 20 dollars' worth of abalone as well.

1723
01:13:35,192 --> 01:13:36,821
All right. I wish you good sales.

1724
01:13:36,822 --> 01:13:39,792
(He's done getting ingredients for dinner energetically.)

1725
01:13:41,332 --> 01:13:44,761
(Shall I go back now?)

1726
01:13:44,762 --> 01:13:46,602
Resuming your workouts.

1727
01:13:48,472 --> 01:13:50,241
(He begins running again with clams in his hands.)

1728
01:13:50,242 --> 01:13:51,342
With clams?

1729
01:13:53,472 --> 01:13:54,942
That's really tiring.

1730
01:13:55,972 --> 01:13:57,082
It's so heavy.

1731
01:13:57,342 --> 01:13:58,411
It was really heavy.

1732
01:13:58,412 --> 01:14:00,011
You're running with 2kg clams?

1733
01:14:00,012 --> 01:14:01,582
(Added weight that wasn't part of his plan)

1734
01:14:02,252 --> 01:14:03,252
Gosh, it's so cold!

1735
01:14:03,482 --> 01:14:06,452
(A back-and-forth running that wasn't part of his plan)

1736
01:14:08,022 --> 01:14:11,622
(He runs at full speed without giving up.)

1737
01:14:12,162 --> 01:14:14,662
Actually, it motivated me even more.

1738
01:14:15,292 --> 01:14:17,301
- "I'm going to do this." - I had to run perfectly...

1739
01:14:17,302 --> 01:14:19,632
- on the way back, - That's right.

1740
01:14:19,932 --> 01:14:21,632
so I'd think I had a good run.

1741
01:14:21,832 --> 01:14:23,072
- That's why... - That's right.

1742
01:14:23,172 --> 01:14:24,472
That'd complete your run.

1743
01:14:25,902 --> 01:14:28,272
(It's too early to get tired.)

1744
01:14:30,642 --> 01:14:31,842
I'm here!

1745
01:14:34,452 --> 01:14:37,352
(Keeping up with the pace until the end)

1746
01:14:39,122 --> 01:14:42,052
(Completed webfoot octopus run without webfoot octopus)

1747
01:14:44,162 --> 01:14:45,162
(Groaning)

1748
01:14:46,062 --> 01:14:51,302
(Trudging back to the tent)

1749
01:14:54,372 --> 01:14:55,401
I'm cold.

1750
01:14:55,402 --> 01:14:57,642
(Bitter)

1751
01:14:58,772 --> 01:15:01,941
That's when exhaustion hit me.

1752
01:15:01,942 --> 01:15:03,112
Let's take a nap.

1753
01:15:04,642 --> 01:15:05,941
(Sprawling out)

1754
01:15:05,942 --> 01:15:07,012
He should rest.

1755
01:15:08,182 --> 01:15:09,212
(Sighing)

1756
01:15:10,752 --> 01:15:12,952
(Goodness)

1757
01:15:14,022 --> 01:15:15,291
(Flapping)

1758
01:15:15,292 --> 01:15:16,562
The wind is strong.

1759
01:15:18,462 --> 01:15:20,662
(Whether it's windy or not,)

1760
01:15:21,892 --> 01:15:25,031
(he passed out gloriously after the webfoot octopus run.)

1761
01:15:25,032 --> 01:15:26,102
It must be tiring.

1762
01:15:26,562 --> 01:15:29,471
(The fate of Type J who went out, relying on his plan only)

1763
01:15:29,472 --> 01:15:31,602
That nap must feel really sweet.

1764
01:15:32,902 --> 01:15:38,112
(Soon, the sun starts to set.)

1765
01:15:41,452 --> 01:15:43,782
(Rustling)

1766
01:15:44,482 --> 01:15:47,622
(Getting up)

1767
01:15:48,652 --> 01:15:50,291
(He got up, shaking off the pain of a failed plan.)

1768
01:15:50,292 --> 01:15:51,322
Is it time for dinner?

1769
01:15:51,562 --> 01:15:53,761
Thirty minutes went by in the blink of an eye.

1770
01:15:53,762 --> 01:15:55,132
(He got up, shaking off the pain of a failed plan.)

1771
01:15:56,292 --> 01:15:59,832
(Pulling himself together)

1772
01:16:01,272 --> 01:16:02,531
He looks even more tired.

1773
01:16:02,532 --> 01:16:04,241
(Looking exhausted)

1774
01:16:04,242 --> 01:16:05,402
He looks so tired.

1775
01:16:08,312 --> 01:16:09,371
All right.

1776
01:16:09,372 --> 01:16:10,842
(Let's get back on track with the plan.)

1777
01:16:11,912 --> 01:16:14,351
(He recomposes himself...)

1778
01:16:14,352 --> 01:16:16,252
(and gets up.)

1779
01:16:17,782 --> 01:16:20,052
(He prepares dinner in earnest.)

1780
01:16:20,622 --> 01:16:23,022
(Moving the table outside first)

1781
01:16:24,262 --> 01:16:27,392
(He neatly sets up the lights too.)

1782
01:16:29,562 --> 01:16:32,862
(He follows through his plan without hesitating.)

1783
01:16:34,402 --> 01:16:37,172
(While he's busy getting ready for dinner...)

1784
01:16:37,472 --> 01:16:38,542
Bae Na Ra.

1785
01:16:38,872 --> 01:16:40,041
- Mr. Actor. - Bae Na Ra.

1786
01:16:40,042 --> 01:16:41,272
You scared me.

1787
01:16:41,855 --> 01:16:43,054
- Mr. Actor. - Bae Na Ra.

1788
01:16:43,055 --> 01:16:44,185
You scared me.

1789
01:16:44,725 --> 01:16:46,054
Hey!

1790
01:16:46,055 --> 01:16:47,055
- What are you preparing? - Come here.

1791
01:16:47,056 --> 01:16:48,095
- Come here. - Who are they?

1792
01:16:48,625 --> 01:16:49,695
Welcome.

1793
01:16:49,925 --> 01:16:51,825
- Thank you for coming all the way. - Not at all.

1794
01:16:52,765 --> 01:16:54,995
I invited my cherished friends.

1795
01:16:56,335 --> 01:16:58,405
They're my friends...

1796
01:16:58,605 --> 01:17:01,175
whom I've known for almost ten years.

1797
01:17:01,575 --> 01:17:03,705
One of them is Kim Do Hyun.

1798
01:17:03,805 --> 01:17:05,605
And the other one is Lim Jung Mo.

1799
01:17:06,375 --> 01:17:07,915
I've known them since my musical ensemble days.

1800
01:17:08,345 --> 01:17:10,215
That means you're really close.

1801
01:17:12,615 --> 01:17:13,985
I bought kimchi and meat.

1802
01:17:14,215 --> 01:17:15,654
(Laughing)

1803
01:17:15,655 --> 01:17:17,385
- I mean... - Gosh, I got food supplies.

1804
01:17:17,485 --> 01:17:19,184
You must've been excited because your friends came.

1805
01:17:19,185 --> 01:17:20,225
He became brighter.

1806
01:17:21,855 --> 01:17:24,565
They brought everything from meat to desserts.

1807
01:17:26,125 --> 01:17:27,735
- I was setting things up. - Can I get changed?

1808
01:17:27,965 --> 01:17:29,435
Yes, get changed in there.

1809
01:17:30,365 --> 01:17:33,005
(He changes into something comfortable right away.)

1810
01:17:33,305 --> 01:17:35,575
- Shall we grill meat right away? - Okay. Let's get started now.

1811
01:17:35,975 --> 01:17:37,104
Let's grill clams here.

1812
01:17:37,105 --> 01:17:39,145
- That... - Shall we grill meat there?

1813
01:17:39,205 --> 01:17:41,214
- You grill meat in a frying pan. - Okay.

1814
01:17:41,215 --> 01:17:42,774
Right? I'll grill scallops.

1815
01:17:42,775 --> 01:17:43,985
- Then... Wait. - Doesn't that sound good?

1816
01:17:44,445 --> 01:17:45,685
We have scissors and knives.

1817
01:17:46,045 --> 01:17:47,784
We see each other so often...

1818
01:17:47,785 --> 01:17:49,984
that we divide roles really fast.

1819
01:17:49,985 --> 01:17:51,855
- Everyone has their roles. - Yes.

1820
01:17:52,255 --> 01:17:53,755
Hey, suddenly...

1821
01:17:54,195 --> 01:17:56,225
- You feel energized? - Now that you're here,

1822
01:17:56,595 --> 01:17:58,765
I feel more confident all of a sudden.

1823
01:18:00,295 --> 01:18:01,735
(Webfoot octopus isn't available yet?)

1824
01:18:02,935 --> 01:18:05,365
- He must've been really hungry. - Friends are the best.

1825
01:18:07,805 --> 01:18:09,205
Actually, I...

1826
01:18:09,745 --> 01:18:11,975
went to buy webfoot octopus earlier...

1827
01:18:12,245 --> 01:18:14,175
because Incheon is famous for it.

1828
